guides.text:
Quickstart

# Connect your first user.

Create an app, add a token endpoint to your backend, and use that token to connect your client.

01

### Create an app in the dashboard

Generate an app client ID and one-time client secret for the product surface that will own conversations. Store the secret in your backend environment.

02

### Create or sync an app user

Your backend owns app user creation. Use a stable product user ID within each app; the same external ID in another app is an independent identity.

```bash
curl -X POST https://api.convokit.app/api/v1/user \
  -H "content-type: application/json" \
  -H "x-client-id: $CONVOKIT_CLIENT_ID" \
  -H "x-client-secret: $CONVOKIT_CLIENT_SECRET" \
  -d '{"id":"user_123","name":"Avery Stone"}'
```

03

### Issue a scoped user token

Protect your token endpoint with your product authentication. Derive identity from the verified session, synchronize the user, and return only the scoped token. The example requires your own authentication middleware.

```javascript
// app is your existing Express app.
// Supply middleware that verifies your product session and sets req.user.
// For cookie sessions, also enforce your product's CSRF protection.
import { requireProductUser } from './your-auth.js'

const clientId = process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_ID
const clientSecret = process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_SECRET
if (!clientId || !clientSecret) throw new Error('Configure ConvoKit server credentials')

async function callConvoKit(path, body) {
  const response = await fetch('https://api.convokit.app/api/v1/' + path, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'content-type': 'application/json',
      'x-client-id': clientId,
      'x-client-secret': clientSecret,
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
    signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),
  })
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('ConvoKit request failed')
  return response.json()
}

app.post('/convokit/token', requireProductUser, async (req, res) => {
  res.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
  const id = req.user?.id // Trusted session identity, NEVER a request-body ID.
  if (typeof id !== 'string' || !id) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Sign in first' })
  }
  if (req.body?.appUserId !== undefined && req.body.appUserId !== id) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'User does not match your session' })
  }

  try {
    await callConvoKit('user', { id, name: req.user.name })
    const result = await callConvoKit('auth/token', { appUserId: id })
    if (typeof result?.data?.token !== 'string' || !result.data.token) {
      throw new Error('Invalid token response')
    }
    // The customer-facing endpoint returns { token }, not ConvoKit's envelope.
    return res.json({ token: result.data.token })
  } catch {
    return res.status(502).json({ error: 'Chat token temporarily unavailable' })
  }
})
```

04

### Use SDK routes from the client

Clients call SDK routes with the app client ID and scoped user token. The app secret never ships to browser or mobile code.

```bash
curl https://api.convokit.app/api/v1/conversations \
  -H "x-client-id: $CONVOKIT_CLIENT_ID" \
  -H "authorization: Bearer $CONVOKIT_USER_TOKEN"
```

Next, [choose your SDK or UI library](https://convokit.app/docs/sdks) and use its connection example with this token endpoint. You do not need to write raw HTTP calls in an SDK-based client.

Building with an AI coding assistant? [Connect the public ConvoKit MCP server](https://convokit.app/docs/mcp) to get official guides, code examples, and an integration plan inside your assistant.

JavaScript SDK

# Use one typed package for browser chat and trusted Node.js operations.

The official JavaScript and TypeScript SDK covers conversations, messages, media, read receipts, typing, presence, and realtime delivery in modern browsers and Node.js 18+.

Published`@convokitapp/sdk 1.1.0`

[View on npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convokitapp/sdk)

### ESM, CommonJS, and first-class TypeScript declarations

The package is public on npm. It supports modern bundlers, browser applications, and Node.js 18 or newer from the same import path.

### Moving from 0.9.0 to 1.0.0

Use `listMessages` and its opaque `nextCursor` for new history views; `getMessages` remains available for older integrations. Observe `sessionState` for connecting and terminal authentication states instead of inferring them from realtime status. Review the [0.9.0 guide](https://convokit.app/docs/javascript-sdk/0.9.0) when maintaining a pinned app or one of the 0.9 UI libraries.

Web UI packages available`@convokitapp/react-ui 0.10.1``@convokitapp/vue-ui 0.10.1`

[Read React UI docs](https://convokit.app/docs/react-ui)[Read Vue UI docs](https://convokit.app/docs/vue-ui)[React npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convokitapp/react-ui)[Vue npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convokitapp/vue-ui)

### React and Vue UI 0.10 support reactions

React and Vue UI 0.10 require `@convokitapp/sdk >=1.1.0 <2.0.0` and provide built-in reaction controls. See the React and Vue guides for SDK-backed and controlled examples. Earlier UI releases keep their own versioned guides and SDK compatibility ranges.

### Install

Add the published package to a JavaScript or TypeScript app.

```bash
npm install @convokitapp/sdk@1.1.0
```

### Two clients, one security boundary

Use `ConvoKitClient` in the browser with a public client ID and scoped token. Use `ConvoKitServerClient` only on your backend; it holds the client secret.

### Configure the browser client

The token provider calls your own authenticated endpoint. Never embed the ConvoKit client secret in a browser bundle. The SDK connects to https://api.convokit.app automatically.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitClient } from '@convokitapp/sdk'

const chat = new ConvoKitClient({
  clientId: 'your-public-client-id',
  tokenProvider: async (appUserId) => {
    const response = await fetch('/api/convokit/token', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ appUserId }),
    })

    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Could not issue chat token')
    return (await response.json()).token
  },
  onRealtimeError: console.error,
})

await chat.connectUser(currentUser.id)
```

### Create the server token endpoint

Synchronize the signed-in app user, then return only their scoped ConvoKit token to the browser.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitServerClient } from '@convokitapp/sdk'
// Your middleware verifies the product session and sets request.user.
// Enforce your product's CSRF protection when using cookie sessions.
import { requireProductUser } from './your-auth.js'

const admin = new ConvoKitServerClient({
  clientId: process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_ID!,
  clientSecret: process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_SECRET!,
})

app.post('/api/convokit/token', requireProductUser, async (request, response) => {
  response.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
  const appUser = request.user // NEVER derive identity from request.body.
  if (!appUser?.id) return response.status(401).json({ error: 'Sign in first' })
  if (request.body?.appUserId !== undefined && request.body.appUserId !== appUser.id) {
    return response.status(403).json({ error: 'User does not match your session' })
  }
  try {
    await admin.upsertUser({ id: appUser.id, name: appUser.name })
    response.json(await admin.issueUserToken(appUser.id))
  } catch {
    response.status(502).json({ error: 'Chat token temporarily unavailable' })
  }
})
```

### Observe the durable session

Read `sessionState` and subscribe to transitions. A terminal authentication failure sets `requiresReauthentication`; transient realtime interruptions remain a separate signal.

```typescript
// The snapshot is safe to read before or after connecting.
const initial = chat.sessionState
const unsubscribe = chat.subscribeSession(() => {
  const state = chat.sessionState
  if (state.status === 'disconnected' && state.requiresReauthentication) {
    returnToSignIn()
  }
})

await chat.connectUser(currentUser.id)
// A new connection attempt, even for the same user, has a new sessionId.
console.log(chat.sessionState.sessionId)

// Dispose this observer when its owning view unmounts.
unsubscribe()
```

### Conversations

Create and manage rooms from the connected user.

```typescript
const conversation = await chat.createConversation({
  participants: [currentUser.id, teammate.id],
  title: 'Launch room',
  description: 'Release coordination',
})

const conversations = await chat.getConversations({ limit: 25 })
const room = await chat.getConversation(conversation.id)

await chat.updateConversationTitle({
  conversationId: room.id,
  title: 'Production launch',
})
await chat.archiveConversation(room.id)
await chat.unarchiveConversation(room.id)
await chat.leaveConversation(room.id)
```

### Inbox previews and unread counts

-   `listInbox` returns rooms newest activity first (latest surviving message, then creation time) with `latestMessage`, `unreadCount`, `unreadCountCapped`, your `readPosition`, `lastReadAt` and `activityAt` per entry.
-   `unreadCount` counts messages from other users after your read position and is exact up to 1,000; a capped count is a lower bound.
-   `getConversations` keeps its creation order.

```typescript
const page = await chat.listInbox({ limit: 30 })

for (const entry of page.entries) {
  const { conversation, latestMessage, unreadCount, unreadCountCapped, isUnread, activityAt } = entry
  renderRow({
    title: conversation.displayTitle,
    preview: latestMessage?.text,
    // A count (or a capped count) is a number; a marker alone is a dot, never an invented count.
    badge: unreadCountCapped || unreadCount > 99 ? '99+' : unreadCount > 0 ? unreadCount : null,
    dot: isUnread && unreadCount === 0 && !unreadCountCapped,
    time: activityAt,
  })
}

// Walk older rooms with the opaque cursor until it is null.
const older = await chat.listInbox({ limit: 30, cursor: page.nextCursor })

// Refetch on both app-wide signals; throttle the activity one.
const structural = chat.realtime.onInboxChanged(chat.clientId, () => refetchInbox())
const activity = chat.realtime.onInboxActivity(chat.clientId, () => scheduleRefetch())
```

### Mark unread

-   `markConversationUnread` flags a room for the current user only: other members, webhooks and read events never see the marker, and `unreadCount` is untouched.
-   The entry then reports `isUnread` true with `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion`; render a numberless dot when the count is 0, never an invented count.
-   Capture `membership.privateStateVersion` from `getConversation` once per open and send it with every acknowledgement of that open, so a mark made later survives a delayed read; `clearConversationUnread` with `ifVersion` clears an empty room the same way.
-   Marker changes reach your other devices through `onInboxActivity`.

```typescript
// Flag the room for the current user only; other members never see the marker.
const state = await chat.markConversationUnread(room.id)
// state: { conversationId, unreadMarkedAt: Date, privateStateVersion }

// Capture the version once, when the room opens (undefined on an older backend).
const opened = (await chat.getConversation(room.id)).membership?.privateStateVersion

// Every acknowledgement of that open carries it: the marker clears only while
// the version is still current, so a mark made after the open survives.
await chat.markConversationRead(room.id, {
  throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
  ...(opened === undefined ? {} : { privateStateVersion: opened }),
})

// An empty room has nothing to acknowledge: clear the marker conditionally instead.
const { cleared } = await chat.clearConversationUnread(room.id, { ifVersion: opened })
// cleared is false, not an error, when nothing was marked or the version moved on.
```

### Messages

Send messages and page through newest-first room history with an opaque cursor. `getMessages` remains only for compatibility.

```typescript
const message = await chat.sendMessage({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'The release is ready.',
})

const page = await chat.listMessages({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  limit: 20,
})

// Pages are newest first; a null cursor means there is no older history.
const older = page.nextCursor === null ? null : await chat.listMessages({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  limit: 20,
  cursor: page.nextCursor,
})

const sameMessage = await chat.getMessage(message.id)
```

### Edit and delete your own messages

-   `editMessage(messageId, { text, revision })` and `deleteMessage(messageId)` are the author operations: only the sender may call them, while still an active READ\_WRITE member (other members' messages and a READ role fail with status 403).
-   Every `Message` carries `revision`, 0 when sent and +1 on every edit by its author or by your server; `isEditedMessage(message)` (`revision > 0`) is the only edited signal, never `updatedAt`.
-   Send the row's `revision` with every edit: a stale one fails with status 409 and code `REVISION_CONFLICT` and nothing is written, so reload with `getMessage`, show the current text and retry with its revision.
-   `text: null` clears the caption of a message with attachments; attachments are never changed by an edit, and a text-only message cannot be emptied.
-   Deleting is unconditional and cannot be undone; files already received or downloaded are not retracted.
-   Both calls need the 0.8 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), never a deleted message.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitError, isEditedMessage } from '@convokitapp/sdk'

// Edit with the revision of the message as the user saw it.
try {
  const edited = await chat.editMessage(message.id, {
    text: 'The release is ready on Tuesday.',
    revision: message.revision,
  })
  render(edited, isEditedMessage(edited)) // true: the revision advanced
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'REVISION_CONFLICT') {
    // Someone else changed it first: reload, show the current text, keep the
    // draft, and retry with current.revision.
    const current = await chat.getMessage(message.id)
  }
}

// Clear the caption of a message with attachments; the attachments stay.
await chat.editMessage(photo.id, { text: null, revision: photo.revision })

// Delete for every member; other devices learn through onMessageDeleted.
await chat.deleteMessage(message.id)
```

### Quoted replies and jump to a message

-   `sendMessage({ replyToMessageId })` quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when you leave it out; every `Message` then carries `replyToMessageId` (absent when the row is not a reply).
-   The reference is write-once — no edit changes it — and a retry with the same `clientMessageId` must repeat the same target or it rejects with status 409.
-   A target in another room, or one that is gone, rejects with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   Quoted text is never copied onto the reply: `getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)` resolves a whole rendered page in one round trip, trimming the IDs, dropping duplicates in first-seen order and splitting the distinct list into requests of 50, so you never chunk.
-   An ID missing from a resolved result is the only deletion signal and is final; a rejected call writes nothing and says nothing about which IDs exist, so retry it on the next page.
-   `getMessageContext(conversationId, { messageId | olderCursor | newerCursor, limit })` returns one window of history, newest first, centred on a message or continued from a cursor — exactly one selector and `limit` 1..100 (default 30), validated before any request.
-   Both cursors come back on every page and are null at that end of the room; a null `newerCursor` was only true at query time, so return to live history through the ordinary newest page.
-   Both calls need the 0.9 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), which is never "the message is gone" — hide the affordances instead.
-   A room you are no longer an active member of answers 404 with code `CONVERSATION_NOT_FOUND`, and a cursor the backend cannot read 400 with code `INVALID_CURSOR`.
-   Sending a quote to an older backend is the one silent case: the message is stored without the reference, so the quote disappears when the send is confirmed.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitError } from '@convokitapp/sdk'

// Quote a message of the same room. The key is omitted when you leave it out,
// so an ordinary send is unchanged.
const reply = await chat.sendMessage({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'Tuesday works for me.',
  replyToMessageId: quoted.id,
})

// One request for the whole rendered page, never one per row. The SDK trims the
// IDs, drops duplicates and splits the distinct list into requests of 50.
const quotedIds = page.messages.flatMap((message) => message.replyToMessageId ?? [])
const previews = quotedIds.length
  ? await chat.getReplyPreviews(conversation.id, quotedIds)
  : []
const previewById = new Map(previews.map((preview) => [preview.id, preview]))

// An ID missing from a RESOLVED result is the only "the quoted message is gone"
// signal: keep the reply and its reference, render an unavailable placeholder,
// and never ask for that ID again. A rejected call means nothing about the IDs.
renderQuote(reply.replyToMessageId, previewById.get(reply.replyToMessageId))

// Open a quoted message that is older than the loaded history.
try {
  const context = await chat.getMessageContext(conversation.id, {
    messageId: quoted.id,
    limit: 30,
  })
  showWindow(context.messages) // newest first, centred on the target

  // Page back toward the newest message; null means that end of the room.
  if (context.newerCursor) {
    const newer = await chat.getMessageContext(conversation.id, {
      newerCursor: context.newerCursor,
    })
    showWindow(newer.messages)
  }
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // The quoted message was deleted: keep the reply and its reference.
  }
}
```

### Images and files

Upload through signed storage URLs, then attach the returned URL.

```typescript
const fileUrl = await chat.uploadMessageMedia({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  bytes: selectedFile,
  fileName: selectedFile.name,
  contentType: selectedFile.type,
})

await chat.sendMessage({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'Attached for review',
  media: [{
    type: selectedFile.type.startsWith('image/') ? 'image' : 'file',
    url: fileUrl,
    name: selectedFile.name,
    size: selectedFile.size,
  }],
})
```

### Realtime subscriptions

Receive typed events and independently dispose each listener. An edit arrives on `onMessage` as an `update` carrying the new `revision` (keep the higher revision when rows meet); a deletion arrives on `onMessageDeleted` as the message ID.

```typescript
const messageSub = chat.realtime.onMessage(conversation.id, {
  // type is insert or update; merge by ID and keep the higher revision.
  onEvent: ({ message }) => upsertMessage(message),
  onStatus: (status) => setConnectionStatus(status),
  onError: console.error,
})
const deletedSub = chat.realtime.onMessageDeleted(
  conversation.id,
  ({ id }) => removeMessage(id), // keep the ID so a late row cannot restore it
)

const typingSub = chat.realtime.onTyping(
  conversation.id,
  ({ userId, isTyping }) => updateTyping(userId, isTyping),
)
const readSub = chat.realtime.onReadReceipt(
  conversation.id,
  ({ userId, readAt, readPosition }) =>
    updateReadState(userId, readPosition, readAt),
)
const presenceSub = chat.realtime.onPresence(
  chat.clientId,
  ({ userId, isOnline, lastSeenAt }) =>
    updatePresence(userId, isOnline, lastSeenAt),
)

await Promise.all([
  messageSub.unsubscribe(),
  deletedSub.unsubscribe(),
  typingSub.unsubscribe(),
  readSub.unsubscribe(),
  presenceSub.unsubscribe(),
])
```

### Publish typing, reads, and presence

-   Keep ephemeral conversation state synchronized.
-   A read names the newest rendered message; omit `throughMessageId` only when no message is rendered, and the position becomes the newest message on the server.
-   Positions never move backward.
-   Add the `privateStateVersion` captured when the room opened to also clear your own unread marker while it is still current (see Mark unread).

```typescript
await chat.sendTyping({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  isTyping: true,
})
// Name the newest message the user has actually seen.
await chat.markConversationRead(conversation.id, {
  throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
})
await chat.updatePresence({ isOnline: true })
```

### Compute read receipts

Seed from each participant's `readPosition` and `lastReadAt`, keep the newest position per user from live read events, and resolve readers with the shared rule: the position decides by conversation order when present, otherwise `lastReadAt` must be at or after `createdAt`.

```typescript
import { covers, readThrough } from '@convokitapp/sdk'

// Seed from persisted participant state: the read position plus the
// acknowledgement time for participants that have no position yet.
const readStateByUserId = new Map(
  conversation.participants.map((participant) => [
    participant.appUserId,
    { readPosition: participant.readPosition, lastReadAt: participant.lastReadAt },
  ]),
)

chat.realtime.onReadReceipt(conversation.id, ({ userId, readAt, readPosition }) => {
  const current = readStateByUserId.get(userId)?.readPosition ?? null
  // Keep the newest position; an event without one only refreshes the time.
  const advanced = readPosition !== null && (current === null ||
    covers(readPosition, { id: current.messageId, createdAt: current.createdAt }))
  readStateByUserId.set(userId, {
    readPosition: advanced ? readPosition : current,
    lastReadAt: readAt,
  })
})

// A position covers the message by (createdAt, id); lastReadAt is the fallback.
const readers = conversation.participants.filter((participant) =>
  participant.appUserId !== message.senderId &&
  readThrough(readStateByUserId.get(participant.appUserId) ?? {}, message),
)
```

### Joining a room by ID

A room ID is not an authorization mechanism. Your backend decides whether the user may join, adds membership, and only then lets the connected browser client load that room.

```typescript
// Server: validate your product's room policy and add the app user.
await admin.addConversationMember(roomId, {
  appUserId: currentUser.id,
  role: 'READ_WRITE',
})

// Browser: after your join endpoint succeeds, load the room by ID.
const room = await chat.getConversation(roomId)
```

### Session and users

Connect one app user, inspect session state, and read app-user records.

`connectUser / disconnectUser`

Starts and disposes the authenticated user and all realtime channels.

`clientId / realtime`

Exposes the public app ID and connected realtime service.

`connected / currentUserId`

Reports the current session without duplicating identity state.

`sessionState / subscribeSession(listener)`

Expose durable disconnected, connecting, and connected snapshots. Each attempt has a new sessionId; terminal failures carry a sanitized errorCode and requiresReauthentication.

`authHeaders / lastUserToken`

Exposes authenticated HTTP context for advanced integrations.

`getUsers / getUser`

Lists app users with pagination or fetches one by ID.

### Conversations

Create, query, list the inbox, rename, archive, restore, leave, and mark rooms read or unread.

`getConversations / getConversation`

Lists active or archived rooms in creation order and loads one room by ID. getConversation also returns your own membership (role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion); capture privateStateVersion when the room opens.

`listInbox({ limit, cursor, archived })`

Lists rooms newest activity first with a preview, unread count and read state per entry, paged by an opaque cursor. limit is an integer from 1 to 100 (default 30), validated before any request; cursor defaults to null and archived to false.

`createConversation`

Creates a room with participants, title, description, and optional image.

`updateConversationTitle`

Changes or clears the participant-facing room title.

`archiveConversation / unarchiveConversation`

Controls the current user’s archived-room state.

`leaveConversation`

Removes the current user from a room.

`markConversationRead(conversationId, { throughMessageId, privateStateVersion })`

Records the read position through the newest message the user has seen (throughMessageId) and emits a receipt when it advances. privateStateVersion, the version captured at open, also clears your unread marker while it is still current; omit it to leave the marker alone.

`markConversationUnread(conversationId)`

Marks the room unread for the current user only and returns the private state (conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion). Every call advances the version; the count is untouched.

`clearConversationUnread(conversationId, { ifVersion })`

Removes your unread marker without acknowledging a message, only while it still has ifVersion when given. Resolves with cleared true or false (a no-op is not an error) plus the current private state.

### Messages and media

Load messages, send structured content, and upload attachments.

`listMessages({ conversationId, limit, cursor })`

Loads newest-first MessagePage results. Pass the opaque nextCursor back for older messages until it is null; limit is an integer from 1 to 100 (default 20).

`getMessages / getMessage`

getMessage retrieves one row. getMessages is retained for offset-pagination compatibility, but new integrations should use listMessages. Every Message carries revision and optional replyToMessageId.

`sendMessage`

Sends text plus image, file, location, or contact media blocks. replyToMessageId quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when unset; the reference is write-once, so a retry with the same clientMessageId must repeat it, and a target that is gone or in another room rejects with MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`editMessage(messageId, { text, revision })`

Author edit: replaces the text of one of the current user’s own messages, or clears the caption of a message with attachments with text null, and resolves with the updated Message (revision + 1, attachments unchanged). revision is the row’s revision as the user saw it; a stale one rejects with status 409 and code REVISION\_CONFLICT, so reload with getMessage and retry. Both keys are always sent; a missing text or a revision outside 0..2147483647 rejects with INVALID\_ARGUMENT before any request.

`deleteMessage(messageId)`

Author delete: removes one of the current user’s own messages for every member and resolves with no value. Unconditional (no revision) and cannot be undone; other devices learn through realtime.onMessageDeleted. A message that is already gone rejects with code MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)`

Resolves the quoted messages a rendered page points at in one round trip, never one request per row. The IDs are trimmed and de-duplicated in first-seen order and the distinct list is split into requests of 50, merged in that order; an empty list, a blank ID or an ID over 64 characters rejects with INVALID\_ARGUMENT before any request. IDs that do not exist, were deleted or belong to another room are simply absent from a resolved result — the only deletion signal — while a rejected call says nothing about which IDs exist.

`getMessageContext(conversationId, { messageId, olderCursor, newerCursor, limit })`

Returns one window of a room’s history as MessageContextPage (messages newest first, olderCursor and newerCursor always present and null at that end of the room). Exactly one of messageId, olderCursor and newerCursor, and limit an integer 1..100 (default 30), validated before any request. A centred window always contains its target; an unknown, deleted or foreign messageId rejects with MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND and an unreadable cursor with INVALID\_CURSOR.

`uploadMessageMedia`

Uploads an attachment and returns the URL to include in a message.

`uploadUserAvatar / deleteUserAvatar`

Assigns or clears an app-user avatar.

`uploadConversationImage / deleteConversationImage`

Assigns or clears a room image.

`downloadMedia`

Downloads protected media through the authenticated proxy.

### Realtime state

Observe messages, typing, receipts, and presence with disposable subscriptions.

`realtime.onMessage`

Streams inserted and updated messages for one conversation as { type, message }; an edit arrives as an update carrying the new revision, so merge by ID and keep the higher revision.

`realtime.onMessageDeleted`

Streams the IDs of deleted messages for one conversation; remove the row and keep the ID so a late response cannot restore it.

`realtime.onTyping`

Streams user typing state.

`realtime.onReadReceipt`

Streams user read positions with their acknowledgement time.

`realtime.onPresence`

Streams online and last-seen events for the app.

`realtime.onInboxChanged`

Signals when your custom inbox should reload after membership, metadata, profile or deletion changes, including after reconnecting.

`realtime.onInboxActivity`

Signals a message sent or edited, a read position advancing, or your own unread marker changing, anywhere in the app. Empty payload, never raised on connection; throttle the reload it triggers.

`sendTyping / updatePresence`

Publishes the current user’s ephemeral UI state.

`subscription.unsubscribe / disconnectUser`

Disposes one listener or the complete signed-in session.

`subscription.closed / realtime.appUserId`

Exposes listener lifecycle and the realtime user identity.

`realtime.dispose`

Removes every subscription owned by the realtime service.

### Server-only API

These operations require `ConvoKitServerClient` and must never run in client-side JavaScript.

`createUser / updateUser / upsertUser / deleteUser`

Synchronize your application’s user lifecycle.

`issueUserToken`

Issue a one-hour scoped SDK token for an authenticated app user.

`updateConversation / deleteConversation`

Administer room title, description, image, or deletion.

`addConversationMember / removeConversationMember`

Apply your product’s room membership policy.

`updateMessage(id, { text?, media?, revision? }) / deleteMessage(id)`

Administrative edit and delete of any message (separate from the author operations on ConvoKitClient). updateMessage replaces text and/or media and increments the message’s revision; pass revision to apply only while the stored value still matches (409 REVISION\_CONFLICT otherwise). deleteMessage resolves with the deleted ID.

### Exported models and events

All public inputs, models, media unions, handlers, and events ship as TypeScript declarations. `Message.revision` is a required member, so consumer-built literals (fixtures, controlled views) gain it.

`AppUser`id, appId, name, imageUrl, lastSeenAt, createdAt, updatedAt

`Conversation`id, title, imageUrl, appId, displayTitle, description, participants, timestamps; membership (your own row) on getConversation results only

`ConversationMembership`role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt (Date | null), privateStateVersion; never part of participants or inbox entries

`Participant`id, appUserId, name, imageUrl, role, lastReadAt, readPosition

`ReadPosition`messageId, createdAt; compare with covers(position, message) or readThrough(reader, message)

`Message`id, conversationId, senderId, clientMessageId, text, media, createdAt, updatedAt, revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit; isEditedMessage(message) is revision > 0), replyToMessageId (the quoted message when the row is a reply, absent otherwise)

`EditMessageInput / isEditedMessage`text (string | null) and revision for editMessage; isEditedMessage(message) is the shared edited rule

`ReplyPreview`id, conversationId, senderId, text (first 500 characters, null when the quoted message has none), textTruncated, createdAt, revision, mediaCount; resolved by getReplyPreviews and never embedded in a Message

`MessageContextPage / MessageContextOptions`MessageContextPage carries messages (newest first) plus olderCursor and newerCursor (always present, null at that end of the room); MessageContextOptions is messageId, olderCursor, newerCursor and limit (1..100, default 30), exactly one selector

`MessagePage / MessagePageOptions`MessagePage carries newest-first messages and nextCursor (string | null); options are conversationId, limit (1..100, default 20) and an opaque cursor

`MessageMedia`image, file, location, and contact discriminated unions

`InboxSummary`latestMessage (Message | null, at most its first 4 media), unreadCount, unreadCountCapped, readPosition, lastReadAt, isUnread, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion, activityAt

`InboxEntry / InboxPage`InboxEntry extends InboxSummary with conversation (participants limited to 10); InboxPage carries entries and nextCursor (string | null)

`InboxListOptions`limit (1..100, default 30), cursor (string | null), archived (default false)

`ConversationPrivateState / ClearUnreadResult`conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion; ClearUnreadResult adds cleared

`MarkConversationReadOptions / ClearConversationUnreadOptions`throughMessageId and privateStateVersion; ifVersion

`Realtime events`MessageEvent (type insert | update, message), MessageDeletedEvent (id, conversationId), TypingEvent, ReadEvent (userId, readAt, readPosition), PresenceEvent, RealtimeStatus

`SessionState / SessionEndReason`Durable disconnected, connecting and connected snapshots with a per-attempt sessionId; terminal disconnected states carry reason, requiresReauthentication and a sanitized errorCode

### Error handling

-   `ConvoKitError` carries a stable code plus HTTP status and response body when available.
-   A read whose `throughMessageId` is not a message in that conversation fails with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   `listInbox` rejects a `limit` outside 1..100 with code `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request, and a cursor ConvoKit did not issue fails with status 400 and code `INVALID_CURSOR`; a page the SDK cannot parse rejects with a plain `TypeError`.
-   A `privateStateVersion` or `ifVersion` that is not an integer in 0..2147483647 is rejected with code `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request; against an older backend the mark and clear calls fail with status 404 and `HTTP_ERROR`.
-   `editMessage` with a stale `revision` fails with status 409 and code `REVISION_CONFLICT` (nothing was written: reload the row with `getMessage` and retry); a missing `text` or a `revision` outside 0..2147483647 is rejected with `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request; another member's message or a `READ` role fails with status 403; a message the caller cannot see, or one already deleted, fails with status 404 and code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` on `editMessage`, `deleteMessage` and `getMessage` alike.
-   Against an older backend the author calls fail with status 404 and `HTTP_ERROR`, which is never a deleted message.
-   Other HTTP failures keep `HTTP_ERROR`.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitError } from '@convokitapp/sdk'

try {
  await chat.markConversationRead(conversationId, { throughMessageId })
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // The target is no longer in this conversation: acknowledge the
    // next newest rendered message instead.
  } else if (error instanceof ConvoKitError) {
    console.error(error.code, error.status, error.responseBody)
  }
}

try {
  await chat.editMessage(message.id, { text: draft, revision: message.revision })
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'REVISION_CONFLICT') {
    // Stale revision: reload the message, show it, and retry with its revision.
  } else if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // Deleted or no longer accessible: remove the row.
  }
}
```

### Session cleanup

Call `disconnectUser()` when the signed-in user changes or signs out. It removes active realtime channels and clears user tokens from the SDK instance.

```typescript
await chat.disconnectUser()
```

### Session lifecycle

Connect the user before creating subscriptions or SDK-backed UI. Your token provider must fetch fresh tokens from your authenticated backend.

On sign-out or account change, dispose the current UI controllers and subscriptions, then disconnect the client. Create a new adapter or controller after the next successful login, even when signing back in as the same user.

See [authentication](https://convokit.app/docs/auth) for the token flow and [messaging behavior](https://convokit.app/docs/messaging) for read receipts, retries, timestamps, and what the SDK-backed UI handles automatically.

React Native SDK

# Build mobile chat with one typed client for bare React Native and Expo.

The React Native SDK bundles the ConvoKit JavaScript client with mobile-safe runtime polyfills, Expo adapters, URI-based uploads, protected downloads, reactive session state, React data hooks, and the complete realtime API.

Published`@convokitapp/react-native`

### Documentation version 1.1.0

-   Requires Node 22.13 or newer and is tested with React 19.2, React Native 0.86–0.87, Hermes, the New Architecture, and Expo 57.
-   The compatible core SDK is bundled as a runtime dependency, so apps install only this package.
-   The package intentionally excludes server-only client APIs and re-exports the core `ReadPosition` type with the `covers` and `readThrough` helpers, the `InboxSummary`, `InboxEntry`, `InboxPage` and `InboxListOptions` types, and the `ConversationMembership`, `ConversationPrivateState`, `ClearUnreadResult` and `ClearConversationUnreadOptions` types.
-   It also re-exports the `EditMessageInput` type with the `isEditedMessage` helper, the cursor-paged `MessagePage` types, and the durable `SessionState` types.
-   App code never imports `@convokitapp/sdk` directly. `Message.revision` is required, including in fixtures and controlled views.

[View on npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convokitapp/react-native)

### Moving from 0.9.0 to 1.0.0

Install only `@convokitapp/react-native`; its compatible core SDK is now a runtime dependency. Use cursor-paged `listMessages` for new history views and the session-aware hooks for React state. React Native UI 0.10.0 requires this SDK's 1.1.0 reaction API; older UI releases keep their documented SDK pairing in the [0.9.0 guide](https://convokit.app/docs/react-native-sdk/0.9.0).

### Install

Install the React Native package. Version 1.1 bundles its compatible JavaScript core SDK, so there is no separate core peer to install or align.

```bash
npm install @convokitapp/react-native@1.1.0

# Expo apps also install the native adapters:
npx expo install expo-crypto expo-file-system
```

### Backend token endpoint

Authenticate your product user here and keep the ConvoKit secret on the backend.

```javascript
// app is your existing Express app.
// Supply middleware that verifies your product session and sets req.user.
// For cookie sessions, also enforce your product's CSRF protection.
import { requireProductUser } from './your-auth.js'

const clientId = process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_ID
const clientSecret = process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_SECRET
if (!clientId || !clientSecret) throw new Error('Configure ConvoKit server credentials')

async function callConvoKit(path, body) {
  const response = await fetch('https://api.convokit.app/api/v1/' + path, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'content-type': 'application/json',
      'x-client-id': clientId,
      'x-client-secret': clientSecret,
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
    signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),
  })
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('ConvoKit request failed')
  return response.json()
}

app.post('/convokit/token', requireProductUser, async (req, res) => {
  res.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
  const id = req.user?.id // Trusted session identity, NEVER a request-body ID.
  if (typeof id !== 'string' || !id) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Sign in first' })
  }
  if (req.body?.appUserId !== undefined && req.body.appUserId !== id) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'User does not match your session' })
  }

  try {
    await callConvoKit('user', { id, name: req.user.name })
    const result = await callConvoKit('auth/token', { appUserId: id })
    if (typeof result?.data?.token !== 'string' || !result.data.token) {
      throw new Error('Invalid token response')
    }
    // The customer-facing endpoint returns { token }, not ConvoKit's envelope.
    return res.json({ token: result.data.token })
  } catch {
    return res.status(502).json({ error: 'Chat token temporarily unavailable' })
  }
})
```

### Configure the mobile client

Use the Expo entry when you want Expo Crypto and FileSystem adapters; otherwise use the default bare React Native entry.

```typescript
// Bare React Native:
import { ConvoKitClient } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

// Expo: import from '@convokitapp/react-native/expo' instead.
const chat = new ConvoKitClient({
  clientId: 'your-public-client-id',
  tokenProvider: async (appUserId) => {
    const productToken = await yourAuth.freshAccessToken()
    const response = await fetch('https://your-api.example.com/convokit/token', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        // Your product token, never a ConvoKit client secret.
        Authorization: `Bearer ${productToken}`,
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({ appUserId }),
    })
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Could not issue chat token')
    return (await response.json()).token
  },
})
```

### Connect and observe a user

-   Connect only after your app knows the authenticated product user.
-   `useConvoKitSession` covers connecting, connected, manual disconnect, user replacement, connection failure, and terminal authentication loss.
-   Temporary realtime interruptions remain a separate signal.

```typescript
import { useEffect } from 'react'
import { useConvoKitSession } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

await chat.connectUser('app-user-123')

function ChatSessionBoundary() {
  const session = useConvoKitSession(chat)

  useEffect(() => {
    if (session.status === 'disconnected' && session.requiresReauthentication) {
      void returnToSignIn()
    }
  }, [session])

  return null
}

// Call this when the product user signs out or changes.
await chat.disconnectUser()
```

### Conversations and messages

-   Create, list, paginate with opaque cursors, send, and report reads through the shared typed API.
-   `listMessages` returns newest-first pages and `nextCursor: null` reliably marks the end; `getMessages` remains only for compatibility.
-   A read names the newest rendered message; omit `throughMessageId` only when no message is rendered, and the position becomes the newest message on the server. Positions never move backward.

```typescript
const conversation = await chat.createConversation({
  participants: ['app-user-123', 'app-user-456'],
  title: 'Product support',
})

const conversations = await chat.getConversations({ limit: 25 })
const page = await chat.listMessages({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  limit: 20,
})

// Pages are newest first. Pass the opaque cursor back to load older history.
const older = page.nextCursor === null
  ? null
  : await chat.listMessages({
      conversationId: conversation.id,
      limit: 20,
      cursor: page.nextCursor,
    })

await chat.sendMessage({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'Can you take a look?',
})

// Acknowledge the newest message the user has actually seen.
await chat.markConversationRead(conversation.id, {
  throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
})
```

### Session-aware React hooks

-   `useMessages`, `useInbox`, and `useTyping` provide focused state without requiring the UI package.
-   They reset on every authenticated session change and ignore stale work from retired sessions.
-   Use their loading and error fields to render retry and pagination states.

```typescript
import { useInbox, useMessages, useTyping } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

const inbox = useInbox(chat, { pageSize: 30 })
const room = useMessages(chat, conversationId, { pageSize: 30 })
const typing = useTyping(chat, conversationId)

await room.sendMessage({ text: draft })
typing.setTyping(draft.length > 0)

// Wire these to the end-reached callbacks in your lists.
if (room.hasMore) await room.loadMore()
if (inbox.hasMore) await inbox.loadMore()

renderConversationList(inbox.entries, {
  loading: inbox.loading,
  loadingMore: inbox.loadingMore,
  error: inbox.error,
})
renderMessages(room.messages, typing.typingUserIds)
```

### Inbox previews and unread counts

-   `listInbox` returns an `InboxPage` of rooms newest activity first (latest surviving message, then creation time).
-   Each `InboxEntry` extends `InboxSummary` (`latestMessage`, `unreadCount`, `unreadCountCapped`, your `readPosition`, `lastReadAt`, `activityAt`) with `conversation`.
-   `unreadCount` counts messages from other users after your read position and is exact up to 1,000; a capped count is a lower bound.

```typescript
const page = await chat.listInbox({ limit: 30 })

for (const { conversation, latestMessage, unreadCount, unreadCountCapped, isUnread, activityAt } of page.entries) {
  renderRow({
    title: conversation.displayTitle,
    preview: latestMessage?.text,
    // A count (or a capped count) is a number; a marker alone is a dot, never an invented count.
    badge: unreadCountCapped || unreadCount > 99 ? '99+' : unreadCount > 0 ? unreadCount : null,
    dot: isUnread && unreadCount === 0 && !unreadCountCapped,
    time: activityAt,
  })
}

// Walk older rooms with the opaque cursor until it is null.
const older = await chat.listInbox({ limit: 30, cursor: page.nextCursor })

// Refetch on both app-wide signals; throttle the activity one.
const structural = chat.realtime.onInboxChanged(chat.clientId, () => refetchInbox())
const activity = chat.realtime.onInboxActivity(chat.clientId, () => scheduleRefetch())
```

### Mark unread

-   `markConversationUnread` flags a room for the current user only: other members, webhooks and read events never see the marker, and `unreadCount` is untouched.
-   `InboxSummary` carries `isUnread` (true for a count, a capped count or the marker), `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion`; render a numberless dot when the count is 0, never an invented count.
-   Capture `membership.privateStateVersion` from `getConversation` once per open and send it with every acknowledgement of that open, so a mark made later survives a delayed read.
-   `clearConversationUnread` with `ifVersion` clears an empty room the same way. Marker changes reach your other devices through `onInboxActivity`.

```typescript
// Flag the room for the current user only; other members never see the marker.
const state = await chat.markConversationUnread(conversation.id)
// state: { conversationId, unreadMarkedAt: Date, privateStateVersion }

// Capture the version once, when the room opens (undefined on an older backend).
const opened = (await chat.getConversation(conversation.id)).membership?.privateStateVersion

// Every acknowledgement of that open carries it: the marker clears only while
// the version is still current, so a mark made after the open survives.
await chat.markConversationRead(conversation.id, {
  throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
  ...(opened === undefined ? {} : { privateStateVersion: opened }),
})

// An empty room has nothing to acknowledge: clear the marker conditionally instead.
const { cleared } = await chat.clearConversationUnread(conversation.id, { ifVersion: opened })
// cleared is false, not an error, when nothing was marked or the version moved on.
```

### Edit and delete your own messages

-   `editMessage(messageId, { text, revision })` and `deleteMessage(messageId)` are the author operations: only the sender may call them, while still an active `READ_WRITE` member. Other members’ messages and a `READ` role fail with status 403.
-   Every `Message` carries `revision`, 0 when sent and +1 on every edit by its author or by your server; `isEditedMessage(message)` (`revision > 0`) is the only edited signal, never `updatedAt`.
-   Send the row’s `revision` with every edit: a stale one fails with status 409 and code `REVISION_CONFLICT` and nothing is written, so reload with `getMessage`, show the current text and retry with its revision.
-   `text: null` clears the caption of a message with attachments; attachments are never changed by an edit, and a text-only message cannot be emptied.
-   Deleting is unconditional and cannot be undone; files already received or downloaded are not retracted. Both calls need the 0.8 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), never a deleted message.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitError, isEditedMessage } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

// Edit with the revision of the message as the user saw it.
try {
  const edited = await chat.editMessage(message.id, {
    text: 'Can you take a look today?',
    revision: message.revision,
  })
  render(edited, isEditedMessage(edited)) // true: the revision advanced
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'REVISION_CONFLICT') {
    // Someone else changed it first: reload, show the current text, keep the
    // draft, and retry with current.revision.
    const current = await chat.getMessage(message.id)
  }
}

// Clear the caption of a message with attachments; the attachments stay.
await chat.editMessage(photo.id, { text: null, revision: photo.revision })

// Delete for every member; other devices learn through onMessageDeleted.
await chat.deleteMessage(message.id)
```

### Quoted replies and jump to a message

-   `sendMessage({ replyToMessageId })` quotes a message of the same room and omits the field when you leave it out; every `Message` then carries `replyToMessageId` when the row is a reply.
-   The reference is write-once—no edit changes it—and a retry with the same `clientMessageId` must repeat the same target or it rejects with status 409. A target in another room, or one that is gone, rejects with `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   Quoted text is never copied onto the reply: `getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)` resolves a whole rendered page in one round trip, dropping duplicates in first-seen order and splitting the distinct list into requests of 50, so you never chunk.
-   An ID missing from a resolved result is the only deletion signal and is final; a rejected call writes nothing and says nothing about which IDs exist, so retry it on the next page.
-   `getMessageContext(conversationId, { messageId | olderCursor | newerCursor, limit })` returns one window of history, newest first, centred on a message or continued from a cursor—exactly one selector and `limit` 1..100 (default 30), validated before any request. A centred window always contains its target.
-   Both cursors come back on every page and are null at that end of the room; a null `newerCursor` was only true at query time, so return to live history through the ordinary newest page.
-   Both calls need the 0.9 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), which is never "the message is gone"—hide the affordances instead. A departed member receives `CONVERSATION_NOT_FOUND`, and an unreadable cursor receives `INVALID_CURSOR`.
-   Sending a quote to an older backend is the one silent case: the message is stored without the reference, so the quote disappears when the send is confirmed.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitError } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

// Quote a message of the same room. The key is omitted when you leave it out,
// so an ordinary send is unchanged.
const reply = await chat.sendMessage({
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'Tuesday works for me.',
  replyToMessageId: quoted.id,
})

// One request for the whole rendered page, never one per row. The SDK trims the
// IDs, drops duplicates and splits the distinct list into requests of 50.
const quotedIds = page.messages.flatMap((message) => message.replyToMessageId ?? [])
const previews = quotedIds.length
  ? await chat.getReplyPreviews(conversation.id, quotedIds)
  : []
const previewById = new Map(previews.map((preview) => [preview.id, preview]))

// An ID missing from a RESOLVED result is the only "the quoted message is gone"
// signal: keep the reply and its reference, render an unavailable placeholder,
// and never ask for that ID again. A rejected call means nothing about the IDs.
renderQuote(reply.replyToMessageId, previewById.get(reply.replyToMessageId))

// Open a quoted message that is older than the loaded history.
try {
  const context = await chat.getMessageContext(conversation.id, {
    messageId: quoted.id,
    limit: 30,
  })
  showWindow(context.messages) // newest first, centred on the target

  // Page back toward the newest message; null means that end of the room.
  if (context.newerCursor) {
    const newer = await chat.getMessageContext(conversation.id, {
      newerCursor: context.newerCursor,
    })
    showWindow(newer.messages)
  }
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // The quoted message was deleted: keep the reply and its reference.
  }
}
```

