### Realtime subscriptions

Subscribe after connecting and always release handles with the owning state.

```typescript
const messages = chat.realtime.onMessage(conversation.id, ({ type, message }) => {
  // type is insert or update; an edit arrives as an update carrying the new
  // revision, so merge by ID and keep the higher revision.
  upsertMessage(message)
})
const deleted = chat.realtime.onMessageDeleted(conversation.id, ({ id }) => {
  removeMessage(id) // keep the ID so a late row cannot restore it
})
const typing = chat.realtime.onTyping(conversation.id, ({ userId, isTyping }) => {
  updateTyping(userId, isTyping)
})
const reads = chat.realtime.onReadReceipt(conversation.id, ({ userId, readAt, readPosition }) => {
  // readPosition is the newest message this user has read; readAt is when they reported it.
  updateReadState(userId, readPosition, readAt)
})

// Dispose subscriptions when their screen or state owner unmounts.
await Promise.all([
  messages.unsubscribe(),
  deleted.unsubscribe(),
  typing.unsubscribe(),
  reads.unsubscribe(),
])
```

### Compute read receipts

-   Seed from each participant's `readPosition` and `lastReadAt`.
-   Keep the newest position per user from live read events.
-   The position decides by conversation order when present; otherwise `lastReadAt` must be at or after `createdAt`.
-   The React Native UI package applies the same rule for you.

```typescript
import { covers, readThrough } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

// Seed from persisted participant state: the read position plus the
// acknowledgement time for participants that have no position yet.
const readStateByUserId = new Map(
  conversation.participants.map((participant) => [
    participant.appUserId,
    { readPosition: participant.readPosition, lastReadAt: participant.lastReadAt },
  ]),
)

chat.realtime.onReadReceipt(conversation.id, ({ userId, readAt, readPosition }) => {
  const current = readStateByUserId.get(userId)?.readPosition ?? null
  // Keep the newest position; an event without one only refreshes the time.
  const advanced = readPosition !== null && (current === null ||
    covers(readPosition, { id: current.messageId, createdAt: current.createdAt }))
  readStateByUserId.set(userId, {
    readPosition: advanced ? readPosition : current,
    lastReadAt: readAt,
  })
})

// A position covers the message by (createdAt, id); lastReadAt is the fallback.
const readers = conversation.participants.filter((participant) =>
  participant.appUserId !== message.senderId &&
  readThrough(readStateByUserId.get(participant.appUserId) ?? {}, message),
)
```

### Session

Create one client, connect the signed-in product user, observe its durable session, and disconnect on logout.

`new ConvoKitClient(options)`

Installs mobile runtime adapters and configures the public client ID and token provider.

`chat.connectUser(appUserId)`

Fetches a scoped token and starts a renewable realtime session.

`chat.disconnectUser()`

Retires the session and disposes its realtime channels.

`chat.sessionState / subscribeSession(listener)`

Expose and observe connecting, connected and disconnected authentication states. Every connection attempt has a new sessionId; a terminal state carries a sanitized errorCode and requiresReauthentication. Realtime channel status remains separate.

`useConvoKitSession(chat)`

Reactively reads the stable sessionState snapshot with React’s external-store contract.

`chat.connected / currentUserId`

Expose the current connection and app-user identity for imperative code.

### Conversations and messages

Use the same typed client API across bare React Native and Expo.

`getConversations / getConversation`

Load conversations in creation order, or one authorized conversation. getConversation also returns your own membership (role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion); capture privateStateVersion when the room opens.

`listInbox({ limit, cursor, archived })`

Load the inbox newest activity first with a preview, unread count and read state per entry, paged by an opaque cursor. limit is an integer from 1 to 100 (default 30), validated before any request; cursor defaults to null and archived to false.

`createConversation`

Create a conversation with app-user participant IDs.

`listMessages({ conversationId, limit, cursor })`

Load a newest-first MessagePage and pass its opaque nextCursor back for older history until it is null. limit is an integer from 1 to 100 (default 20). A cursor remains valid if its message is deleted.

`getMessages / getMessage`

getMessage loads one message. getMessages remains as a deprecated offset-pagination compatibility API; new integrations should use listMessages. Every Message carries revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit by its author or your server) and replyToMessageId when the row quotes another message.

`sendMessage`

Send text and structured media with safe client-message correlation. replyToMessageId quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when unset; the reference is write-once, so a retry with the same clientMessageId must repeat it, and a target that is gone or in another room rejects with MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`editMessage(messageId, { text, revision })`

Author edit: replace the text of one of the current user’s own messages, or clear the caption of a message with attachments with text null, and receive the updated Message (revision + 1, attachments unchanged). revision is the row’s revision as the user saw it; a stale one rejects with status 409 and code REVISION\_CONFLICT, so reload with getMessage and retry. Both keys are always sent; a missing text or a revision outside 0..2147483647 rejects with INVALID\_ARGUMENT before any request.

`deleteMessage(messageId)`

Author delete: remove one of the current user’s own messages for every member. Unconditional (no revision) and cannot be undone; other devices learn through realtime.onMessageDeleted. A message that is already gone rejects with code MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)`

Resolve the quoted messages a rendered page points at in one round trip, never one request per row. The IDs are trimmed and de-duplicated in first-seen order and the distinct list is split into requests of 50, merged in that order; an empty list, a blank ID or an ID over 64 characters rejects with INVALID\_ARGUMENT before any request. IDs that do not exist, were deleted or belong to another room are simply absent from a resolved result — the only deletion signal — while a rejected call says nothing about which IDs exist.

`getMessageContext(conversationId, { messageId, olderCursor, newerCursor, limit })`

Return one window of a room’s history as MessageContextPage (messages newest first, olderCursor and newerCursor always present and null at that end of the room). Exactly one of messageId, olderCursor and newerCursor, and limit an integer 1..100 (default 30), validated before any request. A centred window always contains its target; an unknown, deleted or foreign messageId rejects with MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND and an unreadable cursor with INVALID\_CURSOR.

`archive / unarchive / leave`

Manage the current user’s conversation state and membership.

`markConversationRead / sendTyping`

Record the read position through the newest rendered message (throughMessageId) and broadcast transient typing state. privateStateVersion, the version captured at open, also clears your unread marker while it is still current; omit it to leave the marker alone.

`markConversationUnread(conversationId)`

Mark the room unread for the current user only and receive the private state (conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion). Every call advances the version; the count is untouched.

`clearConversationUnread(conversationId, { ifVersion })`

Remove your unread marker without acknowledging a message, only while it still has ifVersion when given. Resolves with cleared true or false (a no-op is not an error) plus the current private state.

`covers / readThrough`

Re-exported read-position helpers: a ReadPosition covers a message by conversation order; readThrough falls back to lastReadAt for participants without a position.

### React hooks

Use session-aware state helpers when you do not need the higher-level React Native UI package.

`useMessages(chat, conversationId, { pageSize })`

Fetches newest-first history, merges realtime inserts and updates, removes realtime deletions, deduplicates sends, and exposes messages, loading, loadingMore, hasMore, error, refresh, loadMore and sendMessage.

`useInbox(chat, { pageSize, archived })`

Fetches the activity-ordered inbox, refreshes on structural and activity signals, and exposes entries plus loading, pagination, refresh and error state.

`useTyping(chat, conversationId, { remoteIdleMs, localIdleMs })`

Tracks remote typing user IDs, sends local typing transitions, and automatically expires idle indicators. Both idle windows default to 3,000 ms.

`Session changes`

The data hooks clear state when the authenticated session changes and ignore results from retired sessions, including when the same user reconnects with a new sessionId.

### Mobile media

Use URI helpers for picker results, or the shared byte and Blob APIs.

`uploadMessageMediaFromUri`

Reads a device URI and returns both the uploaded URL and ready-to-send media.

`uploadUserAvatarFromUri`

Uploads and assigns a user avatar from a device URI.

`uploadConversationImageFromUri`

Uploads and assigns a conversation image from a device URI.

`saveDownloadedMedia`

Saves protected media when the selected runtime adapter supports it.

### Realtime

Each listener returns an independently disposable subscription.

`realtime.onMessage / onMessageDeleted`

Receive canonical inserts, updates, and deletion IDs. An edit arrives as an update carrying the new revision (merge by ID, keep the higher revision); a deletion arrives as the message ID (remove the row and keep the ID so a late response cannot restore it).

`realtime.onTyping / onReadReceipt`

Receive transient typing and persisted read events; read events carry userId, readAt, and readPosition.

`realtime.onPresence`

Receive online and last-seen changes.

`realtime.onInboxChanged`

Refetch the authorized inbox after membership, metadata, profile or deletion changes, including after reconnecting.

`realtime.onInboxActivity`

Refetch previews, unread counts and your own unread marker after a message is sent or edited, a read position advances or your marker changes anywhere in the app. Empty payload, never raised on connection; throttle the refetch.

`realtime.onConnectionEvent`

Reconcile REST state after a channel joins or rejoins.

### Exported models and events, including hook results

Every public model, input, media union, hook contract, handler and event below ships as a TypeScript declaration from `@convokitapp/react-native`; the Expo entry re-exports the same names, and the server-only client is not part of the package. `Message.revision` is a required member, so consumer-built literals (fixtures, controlled views) gain it.

`AppUser`id, appId, name, imageUrl, lastSeenAt, createdAt, updatedAt

`Conversation`id, title, imageUrl, appId, displayTitle, description, participants, timestamps; membership (your own row) on getConversation results only

`ConversationMembership`role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt (Date | null), privateStateVersion; never part of participants or inbox entries

`Participant`id, appUserId, name, imageUrl, role, lastReadAt, readPosition

`ReadPosition`messageId, createdAt; compare with covers(position, message) or readThrough(reader, message)

`Message`id, conversationId, senderId, clientMessageId, text, media, createdAt, updatedAt, revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit; isEditedMessage(message) is revision > 0), replyToMessageId (the quoted message when the row is a reply, absent otherwise)

`EditMessageInput / isEditedMessage`text (string | null) and revision for editMessage; isEditedMessage(message) is the shared edited rule

`ReplyPreview`id, conversationId, senderId, text (first 500 characters, null when the quoted message has none), textTruncated, createdAt, revision, mediaCount; resolved by getReplyPreviews and never embedded in a Message

`MessageContextPage / MessageContextOptions`MessageContextPage carries messages (newest first) plus olderCursor and newerCursor (always present, null at that end of the room); MessageContextOptions is messageId, olderCursor, newerCursor and limit (1..100, default 30), exactly one selector

`MessagePage / MessagePageOptions`MessagePage carries newest-first messages and nextCursor (string | null); MessagePageOptions is conversationId, limit (1..100, default 20) and an opaque cursor

`MessageMedia`image, file, location, and contact discriminated unions

`InboxSummary`latestMessage (Message | null, at most its first 4 media), unreadCount, unreadCountCapped, readPosition, lastReadAt, isUnread, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion, activityAt

`InboxEntry / InboxPage`InboxEntry extends InboxSummary with conversation (participants limited to 10); InboxPage carries entries and nextCursor (string | null)

`InboxListOptions`limit (1..100, default 30), cursor (string | null), archived (default false)

`ConversationPrivateState / ClearUnreadResult`conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion; ClearUnreadResult adds cleared

`MarkConversationReadOptions / ClearConversationUnreadOptions`throughMessageId and privateStateVersion; ifVersion

`Realtime events`MessageEvent (type insert | update, message), MessageDeletedEvent (id, conversationId), TypingEvent, ReadEvent (userId, readAt, readPosition), PresenceEvent, RealtimeStatus

`SessionState / SessionEndReason`Durable disconnected, connecting and connected snapshots with a per-attempt sessionId; terminal disconnected states carry reason, requiresReauthentication and a sanitized errorCode

`React hooks`UseMessagesOptions / UseMessagesResult, UseInboxOptions / UseInboxResult, UseTypingOptions / UseTypingResult

`Mobile runtime`ReactNativeClientOptions (the core options plus runtimeAdapter), ReactNativeRuntimeAdapter (readFile, optional saveDownload), NativeFileInput (uri, fileName, contentType, size), NativeMessageMediaInput, DownloadedMediaInput

### Error handling

-   Network, authorization, runtime, and validation failures use the exported `ConvoKitError` type.
-   A terminal session snapshot exposes only a sanitized `errorCode`; `requiresReauthentication` tells the app to return the user to sign-in, while transient renewal failures leave a still-valid connected session unchanged.
-   A read whose `throughMessageId` is not a message in that conversation fails with `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`. `listInbox` and `listMessages` reject a `limit` outside 1..100 with `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request; an invalid cursor fails with `INVALID_CURSOR`, and a page the SDK cannot parse rejects with a plain `TypeError`.
-   A `privateStateVersion` or `ifVersion` outside 0..2147483647 is rejected with `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request; against an older backend the mark and clear calls fail with status 404 and `HTTP_ERROR`.
-   `editMessage` with a stale `revision` fails with status 409 and `REVISION_CONFLICT` and nothing is written: reload with `getMessage` and retry with its revision. Another member’s message or a `READ` role fails with status 403; an inaccessible or deleted message fails with `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   Against an older backend the author calls fail with status 404 and `HTTP_ERROR`, which is never a deleted message.

```typescript
import { ConvoKitError } from '@convokitapp/react-native'

try {
  await chat.markConversationRead(conversationId, { throughMessageId })
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // Acknowledge the next newest rendered message instead.
  } else if (error instanceof ConvoKitError) {
    showRetry(error.message, error.code)
  }
}

try {
  await chat.editMessage(message.id, { text: draft, revision: message.revision })
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'REVISION_CONFLICT') {
    // Stale revision: reload the message, show it, and retry with its revision.
  } else if (error instanceof ConvoKitError && error.code === 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // Deleted or no longer accessible: remove the row.
  }
}
```

### Session lifecycle

Connect the user before creating subscriptions or SDK-backed UI. Your token provider must fetch fresh tokens from your authenticated backend.

On sign-out or account change, dispose the current UI controllers and subscriptions, then disconnect the client. Create a new adapter or controller after the next successful login, even when signing back in as the same user.

See [authentication](https://convokit.app/docs/auth) for the token flow and [messaging behavior](https://convokit.app/docs/messaging) for read receipts, retries, timestamps, and what the SDK-backed UI handles automatically.

React Native UI

# Ship native chat components, then replace only the pieces your product owns.

The React Native UI package provides SDK-backed and controlled conversation surfaces for bare React Native and Expo, with inbox previews and unread counts, pagination, optimistic sends, realtime reconciliation, media, read receipts, render callbacks, and platform-neutral themes.

Published`@convokitapp/react-native-ui 0.10.0``@convokitapp/react-native 1.1.0`

### Native defaults without app-framework lock-in

-   The package deliberately owns no navigation, safe-area, picker, filesystem, or Expo dependency.
-   Your application supplies those boundaries through callbacks.
-   It also re-exports the core `Message`, `ReadPosition`, `InboxSummary`, `InboxEntry`, `ConversationMembership`, `ConversationPrivateState`, `ClearUnreadResult`, `ClearConversationUnreadOptions` and `EditMessageInput` types, so custom adapters and controller callers can import them from `@convokitapp/react-native-ui` as well as from `@convokitapp/react-native`, the same way the React web package exports them; apps built with the previous release keep importing them from the mobile SDK.
-   Pair it with the 1.1.0 mobile SDK.

[View on npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@convokitapp/react-native-ui) [Public examples](https://github.com/ConvoKitApp/Convokit-React-Native-UI-Examples) [Core SDK guide](https://convokit.app/docs/react-native-sdk)

### Install both layers

Pin compatible UI, mobile facade, and core SDK versions together.

```bash
npm install @convokitapp/react-native-ui@0.10.0 \
  @convokitapp/react-native@1.1.0 \
  @convokitapp/sdk@1.1.0
```

### Choose the ownership model

-   Start SDK-backed, or bring application-owned state to the view layer.
-   A custom `ConvoKitUiClient` adapter receives the read target as an optional second argument, `markConversationRead(id, { throughMessageId })`; forward it unchanged and reject an unknown target with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` so the controller can acknowledge the next newest message.
-   The adapter may also implement the optional `listInbox({ limit, cursor, archived })` (returning the core `InboxPage`) and `onInboxActivity(handler)`; `DefaultConvoKitUiClient` does.
-   An adapter without `listInbox`, or a custom `pageLoader`, keeps the creation-order list with empty `summaries`.
-   For mark unread, the same options may carry `privateStateVersion`, which a custom adapter must forward unchanged or acknowledgements from its rooms never clear the marker, and the adapter may implement the optional `markConversationUnread?(id)` (returning the core `ConversationPrivateState`) and `clearConversationUnread?(id, { ifVersion? })` (returning `ClearUnreadResult`); `DefaultConvoKitUiClient` does.
-   Without them `markUnread` and `clearUnread` reject, and an empty room keeps its marker.
-   For editing and deleting, the adapter may implement the optional `editMessage?(messageId, { text, revision })` (resolving with the updated core `Message`; reject a stale revision with an error whose `code` is `REVISION_CONFLICT`, a gone message with `code` `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`) and `deleteMessage?(messageId)`; `DefaultConvoKitUiClient` implements both.
-   Without them no action renders and `saveEdit` / `deleteMessage` reject; existing adapter literals keep compiling.

`ConvoKitConversationList``ConvoKitConversation`Own loading, pagination, previews, unread counts and the private unread marker, realtime subscriptions, sending, editing and deleting your own messages, typing, and reads.

`ConvoKitConversationListView``ConvoKitConversationView`Render state and callbacks supplied by your application.

### Plug-and-play mobile flow

Connect the core SDK first, then compose the components with your navigator and platform services.

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react'
import type { Conversation } from '@convokitapp/react-native'
import {
  ConvoKitConversation,
  ConvoKitConversationList,
  ConvoKitUiProvider,
} from '@convokitapp/react-native-ui'

export function ChatScreen() {
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<Conversation | null>(null)

  return (
    <ConvoKitUiProvider>
      {selected ? (
        <ConvoKitConversation
          sdk={chat}
          conversationId={selected.id}
          onBack={() => setSelected(null)}
          onAddAttachment={() => openYourPicker()}
          onAttachmentPress={(_, media) => openMedia(media)}
        />
      ) : (
        <ConvoKitConversationList
          sdk={chat}
          onConversationSelected={setSelected}
        />
      )}
    </ConvoKitUiProvider>
  )
}
```

