### Inbox previews and unread counts

-   The SDK-backed `ConvoKitConversationList` shows each room's latest message, its activity time in the device timezone, and an unread badge.
-   The preview reads `You: …` for your own latest message, `Name: …` for a named sender in a room with more than two participants, and the body alone otherwise; a media-only message reads `Photo`, the file name or `File`, `Location`, or `Contact`.
-   The badge renders while `unreadCount` is above 0 or the count is capped, shows the count up to 99 and `99+` above that or whenever the count is capped, and carries the accessible name `N unread` (`99+ unread` when capped) with the visible label hidden from the accessibility tree; the title uses the heavier weight while unread.
-   A room marked unread with a count of 0 renders a numberless dot instead (see Mark unread).
-   Its color is the `colors.badge` theme token (unset means `primary`).
-   `useConvoKitConversationList` state carries `summaries` (a map from conversation ID to `InboxSummary`), `currentUserId`, and `isRefreshing`; `ConvoKitConversationListView` accepts `summaries` and `currentUserId`, and `renderItem` receives `summary` and `currentUserId` on its `ConversationRowContext` (absent means the previous rows and no `You:` prefix).
-   `conversationPreview` and `unreadBadge` return the default strings for custom rows.
-   Rows arrive in inbox order and pages are merged by conversation ID with the later entry winning, re-sorted by activity, then ID.
-   Activity signals are coalesced into one refetch per `activityRefreshWindowMs` (default 500; 0 refetches on every signal), while membership and metadata changes refetch immediately; pull-to-refresh shows its spinner only for the pull.
-   If the inbox route answers 404, the list falls back to conversation paging without previews for the rest of the session; `loadInitial()` tries again.

```tsx
import {
  ConvoKitConversationListView,
  conversationPreview,
  unreadBadge,
  useConvoKitConversationList,
} from '@convokitapp/react-native-ui'

const { controller, state } = useConvoKitConversationList({
  client: new DefaultConvoKitUiClient(chat),
  activityRefreshWindowMs: 500, // default; 0 refetches on every activity signal
})

<ConvoKitConversationListView
  conversations={state.conversations}
  summaries={state.summaries}
  currentUserId={state.currentUserId}
  onConversationSelected={setSelected}
  onLoadMore={() => controller.loadMore()}
  renderItem={({ conversation, summary, currentUserId, onPress }) => {
    // unreadBadge returns a count label, or { dot: true, accessibilityLabel: 'Unread' }
    // for a room marked unread with nothing new; never an invented count.
    const badge = summary ? unreadBadge(summary) : null
    return (
      <Pressable onPress={onPress}>
        <Text>{conversation.displayTitle}</Text>
        {summary ? <Text>{conversationPreview(conversation, summary, currentUserId)}</Text> : null}
        {badge?.dot ? (
          <View accessibilityLabel={badge.accessibilityLabel} style={styles.unreadDot} />
        ) : badge ? (
          <Text accessibilityLabel={badge.accessibilityLabel}>{badge.label}</Text>
        ) : null}
      </Pressable>
    )
  }}
/>
```

### Mark unread

-   `ConversationListController` (the `controller` from `useConvoKitConversationList`) exposes `markUnread(conversationId)` and `clearUnread(conversationId, { ifVersion? })`.
-   The marker is private to the viewer: other members, webhooks and read events never see it, and `unreadCount` is untouched.
-   `clearUnread` resolves with the server's `cleared` (this request removed a marker), not with whether the room is read; an unmarked room or a stale `ifVersion` resolves `false` without an error.
-   After either response the row's current summary takes `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion` as one unit and `isUnread` is recomputed, only while the response is not older than the stored version, so a delayed response never brings back a marker a newer action removed.
-   A failed request sets `error` and rejects, without evicting rows, so wrap both calls in a `try` / `catch` (`clearUnread` resolves `false` only for a `cleared: false` answer, never for a failure).
-   Once the controller is no longer active (it was disposed, the session ended, or the signed-in user changed since it was bound) both methods send nothing and reject with `ConversationListController is not active`, so a private marker is never written under a replacement login on the shared client.
-   Every `InboxSummary` carries `isUnread`, `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion`.
-   A row is unread (heavier title) when `isUnread`, the count is above 0, or the count is capped; a count or a capped count keeps the numeric badge, and a room unread only through the marker renders a numberless 8-point dot in the badge color with the accessible name `Unread`, never an invented count; `unreadBadge` returns `{ label: "", accessibilityLabel: "Unread", dot: true }` for that case so custom rows draw the same dot.
-   There is no built-in row action: wire it through `renderItem` or a menu.
-   SDK-backed rooms capture the viewer's own `membership.privateStateVersion` once, the first time the room opens (also after a transient first-load failure), never from a later refresh, and send it with every acknowledgement of that open, so reading clears the marker only while the version is still current and a mark made after the open survives until the room is reopened.
-   A room opened with the marker and nothing rendered calls the adapter's `clearConversationUnread` with the captured version once per open, under the same conditions and foreground gating as the load acknowledgement; `cleared: false` is not an error.
-   Marker changes on other devices arrive through the throttled activity refetch.
-   Lists built with the previous release ignore `isUnread` and keep their counts.

```tsx
const { controller, state } = useConvoKitConversationList({
  client: new DefaultConvoKitUiClient(chat),
})

// No built-in row action: call the controller from a custom row or a menu.
<ConvoKitConversationListView
  conversations={state.conversations}
  summaries={state.summaries}
  currentUserId={state.currentUserId}
  onConversationSelected={setSelected}
  renderItem={({ conversation, summary, onPress }) => (
    <View>
      <Pressable onPress={onPress}><Text>{conversation.displayTitle}</Text></Pressable>
      <Pressable onPress={() => controller.markUnread(conversation.id).catch(showRetry)}>
        <Text>Mark unread</Text>
      </Pressable>
    </View>
  )}
/>

// Remove the marker without opening the room, only while it still has the
// version the row shows. Resolves the server's cleared: false is not an error;
// a failed request sets state.error and rejects, like markUnread.
const cleared = await controller.clearUnread(conversation.id, { ifVersion: summary.privateStateVersion })

// SDK-backed rooms capture membership.privateStateVersion when they open and
// send it with every acknowledgement of that open; nothing to wire.
<ConvoKitConversation sdk={chat} conversationId={selected.id} />
```

### Edit and delete your own messages

-   `ConversationController` (and so `useConvoKitConversation`) owns edit mode.
-   `ConversationState` carries `editingMessage` (the message being edited, as the viewer saw it when editing began; `null` outside edit mode) and `canEditMessages` / `canDeleteMessages` (whether the adapter implements the members); the controller exposes `startEditing(messageId)`, `cancelEditing()`, `saveEdit(text)` and `deleteMessage(messageId)` (both resolve a boolean).
-   `startEditing` is a no-op for another member's row, a pending row, a removed row, a `READ` role or an adapter without `editMessage`; it sends nothing, not even a typing update.
-   `saveEdit` trims the text and sends the revision captured when editing began, never the live row's, so the server compares against what the viewer saw.
-   A stale revision (409 `REVISION_CONFLICT`) reloads the row once through `getMessage`: the row shows the current content, the snapshot moves to it so the banner shows what changed and the next save carries the fresh revision, `error` carries the conflict and the edited text stays in the composer.
-   The same state is entered without a request when a newer revision of the edited row arrives while editing.
-   A 404 with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` on the save or the reload removes the row and ends edit mode; any other failure (403, network, or an uncoded 404 from an older backend) keeps the row, the draft and edit mode and surfaces through `error` without evicting history.
-   `deleteMessage` is never optimistic: the row goes once the adapter resolves or answers `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`, and stays on any other failure; late responses and updates for a removed row are dropped, and a removal by any path ends edit mode on it.
-   When rows for one message meet, the higher `revision` wins and a lower one never overwrites; equal revisions keep the timestamp rule.
-   Default rows: an eligible row (the view was given `onEditMessage` / `onDeleteMessage`, the row is the viewer's own and confirmed, the role is not `READ`) is wrapped in a long-pressable with the `Message actions` accessibility action and hint; a long press opens a sheet with `Edit message`, `Delete message` and `Cancel`, and deleting confirms with `Delete this message?` (`Delete` / `Cancel`; dismissing declines).
-   Pass `confirmDelete(message)` to replace the dialog and `canEditMessage(message)` to replace the own-and-writable rule for both actions (pending rows stay ineligible).
-   Edited rows (`revision` above 0, never pending rows) show `Edited` (accessible name `Edited`) beside the time, for any sender; rows that are not eligible render exactly as before.
-   Default composer: while `editingMessage` is set the unsent draft is stashed and the field is prefilled with the message text without a typing update, a polite live-region banner reads `Editing message` with the original text beside `Cancel` (accessible name `Cancel editing`), and the primary action reads `Save` with the accessible name `Save message` (`Send message` otherwise), enabled while the trimmed field is non-empty or the edited message has attachments, so saving an empty field on a message with attachments sends `text: null` and clears the caption while every attachment stays; a text-only message can never be saved empty.
-   Author edits change text only, so the `Add attachment` control is hidden while editing.
-   Cancel and a successful save restore the stash and report typing for it; a failed save keeps the text and edit mode; when the host leaves edit mode externally the field keeps user-changed text and restores the stash only when it is empty or unchanged.
-   `renderComposer` receives the additive `editing` (the message) and `cancelEdit` on its `ComposerContext` while editing, and its `send()` saves then, so custom composers need no branching.
-   Controlled views: `ConvoKitMessageListView` accepts `onEditMessage(message)`, `onDeleteMessage(message)` (`false` reports that nothing was deleted), `canEditMessage` and `confirmDelete`; `ConvoKitConversationView` adds `editingMessage`, `onSaveEdit(message, text)` (`false` keeps edit mode and the text, like `onSendMessage`) and `onCancelEdit`.
-   Without the callbacks the markup is byte-identical to the previous release.
-   Custom rows receive `isEdited`, `canEdit`, `canDelete` and, only while allowed, `edit()` and `remove()` on `MessageRowContext`.
-   `remove()` asks `confirmDelete` only when you provided one and otherwise calls `onDeleteMessage` directly, so a custom row owns any other confirmation UI; it resolves whether the message was deleted.
-   Only the default row falls back to the built-in `Delete this message?` dialog when no `confirmDelete` is given.
-   The bound `ConvoKitConversation` wires the controller only when the adapter supports the members and passes `confirmDelete` and `canEditMessage` through.
-   Deleting a message removes it and its attachments from the conversation for every member and cannot be undone; files already received or downloaded cannot be retracted.
-   Consumer-built `Message` literals gain the required `revision` member.
-   Clients built with the previous release ignore `revision` and show no actions; against an older backend every save and delete fails with an uncoded 404 that keeps the row and the draft, and every row reads as revision 0.

```tsx
// SDK-backed: own confirmed rows offer Message actions on a long press, the
// composer saves while editing, and confirmDelete replaces the built-in dialog.
<ConvoKitConversation
  sdk={chat}
  conversationId={selected.id}
  confirmDelete={(message) => askTheUser(`Delete "${message.text ?? 'this message'}"?`)}
/>

// Controlled: edit mode is a pure function of editingMessage and the callbacks.
// Leave them out and no action renders.
const { controller, state } = useConvoKitConversation({
  conversationId,
  client: new DefaultConvoKitUiClient(chat),
})

<ConvoKitConversationView
  conversation={state.conversation!}
  messages={state.messages}
  currentUserId={state.currentUserId}
  onSendMessage={({ text }) => controller.sendMessage({ text }).then(Boolean)}
  readPositionByUserId={state.readPositionByUserId}
  editingMessage={state.editingMessage}
  onEditMessage={(message) => controller.startEditing(message.id)}
  onSaveEdit={(_message, text) => controller.saveEdit(text)}
  onCancelEdit={() => controller.cancelEditing()}
  onDeleteMessage={(message) => controller.deleteMessage(message.id)}
  renderMessage={({ message, isEdited, edit, remove }) => (
    <View>
      <Text>{message.text}</Text>
      {isEdited ? <Text accessibilityLabel="Edited">Edited</Text> : null}
      {edit ? <Pressable onPress={edit}><Text>Edit</Text></Pressable> : null}
      {/* Without confirmDelete on the view, remove() deletes at once: confirm here or pass one. */}
      {remove ? <Pressable onPress={() => void remove()}><Text>Delete</Text></Pressable> : null}
    </View>
  )}
  renderComposer={({ value, setValue, send, editing, cancelEdit }) => (
    <View>
      {editing ? <Pressable onPress={cancelEdit}><Text>Cancel editing</Text></Pressable> : null}
      <TextInput value={value} onChangeText={setValue} />
      <Pressable onPress={send}><Text>{editing ? 'Save' : 'Send'}</Text></Pressable>
    </View>
  )}
/>
```

### Quoted replies and jump to a message

-   `ConversationController` (and so `useConvoKitConversation`) owns the reply target and the history window.
-   `ConversationState` carries `replyTarget`, `replyPreviews` (an id to `ReplyPreview | 'unavailable'` map), `windowMode` (`'live' | 'jumped'`), `highlightedMessageId`, `hasNewerMessages`, `isLoadingNewer`, `canJumpToMessages` and `canResolveReplyPreviews`; the controller exposes `startReply(messageId)`, `cancelReply()`, `jumpToMessage(messageId)`, `loadNewerMessages()`, `returnToLatest()` and `clearHighlight()`, with the options `replyPreviewWindowMs` (default 250) and `highlightDurationMs` (default 2000).
-   Any member may quote any confirmed row, not only the caller's own; pending, removed and unknown rows and a `READ` role are refused, deleting the target row clears it, and editing and replying are mutually exclusive.
-   `sendMessage()` carries the target's id, stamps it on the optimistic row so the quoted block renders before acknowledgement, and clears the target on success; a failed send keeps the draft and the quote, and unlike edit mode the draft is never stashed.
-   Quoted parents are re-read, never copied: one `getReplyPreviews` request per page load, reconcile and burst of live inserts — never one per row — covers the distinct references the loaded window cannot derive, while a parent already on screen is derived locally (text cut at 500 characters with `textTruncated` set) and costs nothing.
-   A missing key is the distinct "not yet resolved" state — render the reference with no quoted text, never the unavailable copy: an id absent from a batch that resolved becomes the terminal `'unavailable'`, while a batch that rejects writes no entry at all, surfaces through `error` and is retried on the next trigger.
-   Entries are invalidated by a deletion of that id, by an edit of that row and by a reconnect, and entries no rendered row references are dropped.
-   A target already in the window is only highlighted; anything else replaces the window with one centred `getMessageContext` page and enters `jumped` mode, where both ends page through the context cursors.
-   A jump is a window operation, never a re-open: the acknowledgement floor, the tombstones, the private state captured when the room opened, the edit session and the reply target all survive it, and a coded 404 `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` marks that preview `'unavailable'` instead of erroring.
-   While jumped, realtime inserts are recorded but not rendered and no read is acknowledged (the newest rendered row is not the room's newest); edits, revisions and tombstones for rows inside the window still apply.
-   `returnToLatest()` drains the recorded rows into the rendered set, and acknowledges them, at the moment it switches to `live` — before the newest-page request, so inserts arriving during it merge under the usual precedence; a newer page that reports no newer cursor runs `returnToLatest()` rather than flipping in place, and a failed reload stays `jumped` with the window intact.
-   `sendMessage()` awaits `returnToLatest()` first while jumped and does not send if it fails, leaving `isSending` false and the draft and the reply target untouched.
-   A queued reconcile of a jumped window re-reads the window with one bounded, centred request anchored at the jump target (or at the window's midpoint once it has been paged), tombstones only inside the range the response returned, and leaves the owed tail reconcile owed so it runs on the return to live.
-   Default rows show `Reply` in the long-press `Message actions` sheet ahead of `Edit message` and `Delete message`, and a row carrying a reference renders a quoted block above its text — the parent's author and text (or its attachment count), `Original message unavailable` once the parent is gone, or the reference alone while it is not yet resolved — activatable while `onJumpToMessage` is given, including once the parent is gone.
-   A row whose only would-be action is unavailable is not wrapped in a long-pressable and opens no action sheet, so the sheet never offers `Cancel` alone; conversely, because any member may quote any row, a room where the viewer can reply now makes every confirmed row long-pressable, including other members' messages.
-   The default composer shows a cancellable reply strip (a polite live region) reading `Replying to` the author with `Cancel` (accessible name `Cancel reply`) while `replyTarget` is set, and the primary action stays `Send message`.
-   `ConvoKitConversationView` renders a `Jump to latest` control (accessible name `Jump to latest messages`) exactly when `onReturnToLatest` is given, and `ConvoKitMessageListView` gains a newer-edge pagination trigger on the list's start edge plus a `Loading newer messages` indicator there; both are inert unless `hasNewerMessages` is true, which only a jumped window reports.
-   `ConvoKitUiTheme.colors.highlight` tints the jumped-to row; unset means the accent at low opacity, exactly as `colors.badge` falls back to `colors.primary`.
-   The highlight lasts about two seconds, the move is announced through `AccessibilityInfo`, and a drag clears it early.
-   Scrolling to a row uses `scrollToIndex` against the rendered list with a new `onScrollToIndexFailed` that nudges to an estimated offset and re-attempts at most three times, and `MessageRowContext.chronologicalIndex` keeps the value it has always carried.
-   Controlled views: `MessageListViewProps` gains `onReplyToMessage`, `replyPreviewByMessageId`, `onJumpToMessage`, `highlightedMessageId`, `hasNewerMessages`, `isLoadingNewer`, `onLoadNewer` and `onHighlightDismissed`; `ConversationViewProps` adds `replyTarget`, `onCancelReply` and `onReturnToLatest`.
-   Without the new callbacks the rendered markup is the previous release's markup.
-   `MessageRowContext` gains the flat siblings `canReply`, `reply?`, `replyPreview?` and `jumpToReplyTarget?`, and `ComposerContext` gains `replying?` and `cancelReply?` (flat, like `editing` / `cancelEdit`).
-   `ConvoKitUiClient` gains the optional `getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)` and `getMessageContext(conversationId, options)`, and its `sendMessage` input gains the optional `replyToMessageId`; `DefaultConvoKitUiClient` implements all three, adapters without the two new members keep compiling, and an older adapter still satisfies the widened `sendMessage`.
-   The package re-exports `ConversationWindowMode` and `ReplyPreviewEntry`, and the core `MessageContextOptions`, `MessageContextPage` and `ReplyPreview` types.
-   Against an older backend both new routes answer with an uncoded 404, which is never read as "message gone": after the first such rejection the matching capability flag turns false for the life of the controller and the affordances disappear instead of failing repeatedly.
-   Sending a quote to an older backend degrades visibly and is not detected: the backend parses only `text` and `media`, so it drops the unknown `replyToMessageId` and stores the message with no reference — the optimistic row shows the quote and the confirmed row replaces it without one.
-   The message is delivered; only the reference is lost.

```tsx
// SDK-backed: confirmed rows offer Reply in the long-press sheet, quoted blocks
// resolve themselves in one batched request per page, and activating one jumps.
<ConvoKitConversation sdk={chat} conversationId={selected.id} />

// Controlled: reply and jump state stays controller-owned. Leave the callbacks
// out and nothing renders.
const { controller, state } = useConvoKitConversation({
  conversationId,
  client: new DefaultConvoKitUiClient(chat),
})

<ConvoKitConversationView
  conversation={state.conversation!}
  messages={state.messages}
  currentUserId={state.currentUserId}
  onSendMessage={({ text }) => controller.sendMessage({ text }).then(Boolean)}
  replyTarget={state.replyTarget}
  onReplyToMessage={(message) => controller.startReply(message.id)}
  onCancelReply={() => controller.cancelReply()}
  replyPreviewByMessageId={state.replyPreviews}
  onJumpToMessage={(messageId) => controller.jumpToMessage(messageId)}
  highlightedMessageId={state.highlightedMessageId}
  onHighlightDismissed={() => controller.clearHighlight()}
  hasNewerMessages={state.hasNewerMessages}
  isLoadingNewer={state.isLoadingNewer}
  onLoadNewer={() => controller.loadNewerMessages()}
  onReturnToLatest={state.windowMode === 'jumped' ? () => controller.returnToLatest() : undefined}
  renderMessage={({ message, canReply, reply, replyPreview, jumpToReplyTarget }) => (
    <View>
      {/* Three states, and the third is not the second: resolved, gone, and not
          resolved yet (the reference with no quoted text). */}
      {message.replyToMessageId ? (
        <Pressable onPress={jumpToReplyTarget} disabled={!jumpToReplyTarget}>
          <Text>
            {replyPreview === 'unavailable'
              ? 'Original message unavailable'
              : replyPreview?.text ?? 'Quoted message'}
          </Text>
        </Pressable>
      ) : null}
      <Text>{message.text}</Text>
      {canReply && reply ? <Pressable onPress={reply}><Text>Reply</Text></Pressable> : null}
    </View>
  )}
  renderComposer={({ value, setValue, send, replying, cancelReply }) => (
    <View>
      {replying ? <Pressable onPress={cancelReply}><Text>Cancel reply</Text></Pressable> : null}
      <TextInput value={value} onChangeText={setValue} />
      <Pressable onPress={send}><Text>Send</Text></Pressable>
    </View>
  )}
/>
```

### Filtering and pagination

-   Filter by query, archive state, participant, predicate, or custom order.
-   The controller continues paging when a local filter hides a page.
-   SDK-backed lists arrive in inbox order (latest surviving message, then creation time); setting `comparator` replaces that order for the whole list.

```typescript
const list = new ConversationListController({
  client: new DefaultConvoKitUiClient(chat),
  pageSize: 25,
  initialFilter: { archived: false },
})

await list.setQuery('design')
await list.setFilter({
  archived: false,
  participantIds: new Set(['app-user-42']),
  predicate: (conversation) => conversation.description !== null,
  comparator: (a, b) => a.displayTitle.localeCompare(b.displayTitle),
})
```

