### Optimistic sends and reconciliation

-   The conversation controller inserts a pending message, correlates the server response by client message ID, merges realtime updates, and preserves deletion tombstones.
-   An open room also subscribes to `onInboxChanged` and queues a refresh on every signal, coalesced with the refresh that follows a channel rejoin or a return to the foreground, so a title or membership change, or a deletion whose room notification was missed, is reconciled without reopening the room.
-   Every refresh refetches the viewed range and tombstones each previously known, confirmed message that is no longer in it, so a late send or edit response, a single-message reload or a realtime update cannot bring back a message deleted while the app was away; messages older than the viewed range are never tombstoned, and tombstones last until the room is loaded afresh (the next `loadInitial()`).

### Read receipts and typing

-   Reads are positions.
-   Controllers seed `readPositionByUserId` from each participant's `readPosition`, advance it from live read events, and keep `readAtByUserId` (acknowledgement times) as the fallback for participants without a position.
-   SDK-backed screens acknowledge the newest rendered, confirmed message, only while the app is in the foreground; a read held back in the background is sent when the app returns, and every acknowledgement carries the `privateStateVersion` captured when the room opened so reading clears the viewer's own unread marker only while it is still current.
-   With both `markReadOnLoad` and `markReadOnReceive` off, the controller never sends a read on its own; only an explicit `markRead()` call does.
-   If the server no longer knows the target (`MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`), or the acknowledged or in-flight target is deleted, the controller acknowledges the next newest rendered row once, but a deletion re-targets only where a receive acknowledgement would have been sent anyway: with `markReadOnReceive` off, a deletion never causes an acknowledgement, and an explicit `markRead()` still works.
-   By default, pending rows show Sending…, a confirmed message without readers shows only its timestamp, and read state shows Read by N; ConvoKit does not currently report recipient delivery.
-   Typing broadcasts renew while active and expire automatically.

```tsx
// useConvoKitConversation reports AppState for you. A controller you own
// needs the same hook so reads wait until the app is in the foreground.
const controller = useMemo(() => new ConversationController({
  conversationId,
  client: new DefaultConvoKitUiClient(chat),
  markReadOnLoad: true,
  markReadOnReceive: true,
}), [conversationId])
useConvoKitVisibility(controller)

// Read positions (by conversation order) plus acknowledgement times as
// the fallback for participants without a position.
const readerIds = controller.readerIdsFor(message)

<ConvoKitConversationView
  // ...required room state and callbacks
  readPositionByUserId={state.readPositionByUserId}
  readAtByUserId={state.readAtByUserId}
  renderReadReceipt={(message, readerIds) => (
    <ReaderAvatars userIds={[...readerIds]} />
  )}
/>
```

