### App lifecycle

-   `useConvoKitConversation` and `ConvoKitConversation` report `AppState` to the controller through `setVisible`, refresh when React Native returns to the active state, and dispose subscriptions on unmount.
-   Controllers also expose explicit `dispose()` methods.

Security boundary

### The client secret never belongs in a React Native bundle.

Give the app only a public client ID. Your authenticated backend owns user synchronization, scoped token issuance, membership policy, and the ConvoKit client secret.

### Session lifecycle

Connect the user before creating subscriptions or SDK-backed UI. Your token provider must fetch fresh tokens from your authenticated backend.

On sign-out or account change, dispose the current UI controllers and subscriptions, then disconnect the client. Create a new adapter or controller after the next successful login, even when signing back in as the same user.

See [authentication](https://convokit.app/docs/auth) for the token flow and [messaging behavior](https://convokit.app/docs/messaging) for read receipts, retries, timestamps, and what the SDK-backed UI handles automatically.

Flutter SDK

# Install the published Flutter SDK and build a complete ConvoKit chat flow.

Use the Flutter SDK to connect an app user, work with conversations and messages, upload media, and subscribe to realtime events without shipping app secrets to the client.

Published`convokit_flutter`

### Documentation version 0.10.0

This page documents the Flutter API surface for **convokit\_flutter 0.10.0**. Use the version badge when comparing docs with a package pinned in a Flutter app.

### Install

Pin the published package from pub.dev in your Flutter app.

```yaml
dependencies:
  convokit_flutter: ^0.10.0
```

### Backend token endpoint

Supply your product authentication middleware, derive identity from its verified session, and return a scoped token to Flutter. Keep the ConvoKit client secret on your backend.

```javascript
// app is your existing Express app.
// Supply middleware that verifies your product session and sets req.user.
// For cookie sessions, also enforce your product's CSRF protection.
import { requireProductUser } from './your-auth.js'

const clientId = process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_ID
const clientSecret = process.env.CONVOKIT_CLIENT_SECRET
if (!clientId || !clientSecret) throw new Error('Configure ConvoKit server credentials')

async function callConvoKit(path, body) {
  const response = await fetch('https://api.convokit.app/api/v1/' + path, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'content-type': 'application/json',
      'x-client-id': clientId,
      'x-client-secret': clientSecret,
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
    signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),
  })
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('ConvoKit request failed')
  return response.json()
}

app.post('/convokit/token', requireProductUser, async (req, res) => {
  res.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
  const id = req.user?.id // Trusted session identity, NEVER a request-body ID.
  if (typeof id !== 'string' || !id) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Sign in first' })
  }
  if (req.body?.appUserId !== undefined && req.body.appUserId !== id) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'User does not match your session' })
  }

  try {
    await callConvoKit('user', { id, name: req.user.name })
    const result = await callConvoKit('auth/token', { appUserId: id })
    if (typeof result?.data?.token !== 'string' || !result.data.token) {
      throw new Error('Invalid token response')
    }
    // The customer-facing endpoint returns { token }, not ConvoKit's envelope.
    return res.json({ token: result.data.token })
  } catch {
    return res.status(502).json({ error: 'Chat token temporarily unavailable' })
  }
})
```

### Configure the SDK

Call `ConvoKit.configure` once during app bootstrap. The token provider receives an app user ID and returns a ConvoKit user token. The SDK uses https://api.convokit.app automatically.

```dart
import 'dart:convert';

import 'package:convokit_flutter/convokit_flutter.dart';
import 'package:http/http.dart' as http;

Future<void> configureConvoKit() async {
  ConvoKit.configure(
    clientId: 'your-convokit-client-id',
    tokenProvider: (appUserId) async {
      // Integrate your product authentication service here.
      final productToken = await yourAuth.freshAccessToken();
      final response = await http.post(
        Uri.parse('https://your-api.example.com/convokit/token'),
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          // Your product access token, NOT a ConvoKit app secret.
          'Authorization': 'Bearer $productToken',
        },
        body: jsonEncode({'appUserId': appUserId}),
      );

      if (response.statusCode != 200) {
        throw Exception('Failed to fetch ConvoKit token');
      }

      final body = jsonDecode(response.body) as Map<String, dynamic>;
      return body['token'] as String;
    },
  );
}
```

### Connect a user

Connect after your app has identified the current user. The SDK initializes realtime auth during this step.

```dart
await ConvoKit.connectUser('app-user-123');

// Later, when the user signs out:
await ConvoKit.disconnectUser();
```

### Conversations

Create, list, rename, archive, restore, and leave conversations.

```dart
final conversations = await ConvoKit.getConversations(limit: 20);

final conversation = await ConvoKit.createConversation(
  participants: ['app-user-123', 'app-user-456'],
  title: 'Product support',
);

await ConvoKit.updateConversationTitle(
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  title: 'Billing support',
);

await ConvoKit.archiveConversation(conversation.id);
await ConvoKit.unarchiveConversation(conversation.id);
await ConvoKit.leaveConversation(conversation.id);
```

### Inbox previews and unread counts

-   `listInbox` returns an `InboxPage` of rooms newest activity first (latest surviving message, then creation time).
-   Each `InboxEntry` pairs the `conversation` with an `InboxSummary`: `latestMessage`, `unreadCount`, `unreadCountCapped`, the caller’s `readPosition` and `lastReadAt`, and `activityAt`.
-   `unreadCount` counts messages from other users after your read position and is exact up to 1,000; a capped count is a lower bound.
-   `limit` defaults to 30 and must be 1..100; `cursor` is omitted when null.

```dart
final page = await ConvoKit.listInbox(limit: 30);

for (final entry in page.entries) {
  final summary = entry.summary;
  renderRow(
    title: entry.conversation.displayTitle,
    preview: summary.latestMessage?.text,
    // A count (or a capped count) is a number; a marker alone is a dot,
    // never an invented count.
    badge: summary.unreadCountCapped || summary.unreadCount > 99
        ? '99+'
        : summary.unreadCount > 0
            ? summary.unreadCount.toString()
            : null,
    dot: summary.isUnread &&
        summary.unreadCount == 0 &&
        !summary.unreadCountCapped,
    time: summary.activityAt,
  );
}

// Walk older rooms with the opaque cursor until it is null.
if (page.nextCursor != null) {
  final older = await ConvoKit.listInbox(cursor: page.nextCursor);
}

// Refetch on both app-wide signals; throttle the activity one.
final changesSub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onInboxChanged(ConvoKit.clientId)
    .listen((_) => reloadInbox());
final activitySub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onInboxActivity(ConvoKit.clientId)
    .listen((_) => scheduleReload());
```

### Mark unread

-   `markConversationUnread` flags a room for the current user only: other members, webhooks and read events never see the marker, and `unreadCount` is untouched.
-   `InboxSummary` carries `isUnread` (true for a count, a capped count or the marker), `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion`; render a numberless dot when the count is 0, never an invented count.
-   Capture `membership?.privateStateVersion` from `getConversation` once per open and send it with every acknowledgement of that open, so a mark made later survives a delayed read; `clearConversationUnread` with `ifVersion` clears an empty room the same way.
-   Marker changes reach your other devices through `onInboxActivity`.

```dart
// Flag the room for the current user only; other members never see the marker.
final state = await ConvoKit.markConversationUnread(conversation.id);
// state.unreadMarkedAt, state.privateStateVersion

// Capture the version once, when the room opens (null on an older backend).
final opened =
    (await ConvoKit.getConversation(conversation.id)).membership?.privateStateVersion;

// Every acknowledgement of that open carries it: the marker clears only while
// the version is still current, so a mark made after the open survives.
await ConvoKit.markConversationRead(
  conversation.id,
  throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
  privateStateVersion: opened,
);

// An empty room has nothing to acknowledge: clear the marker conditionally instead.
final result = await ConvoKit.clearConversationUnread(
  conversation.id,
  ifVersion: opened,
);
// result.cleared is false, not an error, when nothing was marked or the version moved on.
```

### Messages

Send text messages and load message history with pagination.

```dart
final message = await ConvoKit.sendMessage(
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'Can you take a look?',
);

final messages = await ConvoKit.getMessages(
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  limit: 50,
);
```

### Edit and delete your own messages

-   `ConvoKit.editMessage(id, text: newText, revision: message.revision)` and `ConvoKit.deleteMessage(id)` are the author operations: only the sender may call them, while still an active READ\_WRITE member (other members' messages and a READ role fail with status 403, a `ConvoKitAuthException`).
-   Every `Message` carries `revision`, 0 when sent and +1 on every edit by its author or by your server; `isEdited` (`revision > 0`) is the only edited signal, never `updatedAt`.
-   Send the row's `revision` with every edit: a stale one fails with status 409 and code `REVISION_CONFLICT` (a `ConvoKitValidationException`) and nothing is written, so reload with `getMessage`, show the current text and retry with its revision.
-   A null text clears the caption of a message with attachments; attachments are never changed by an edit, and a text-only message cannot be emptied.
-   Deleting is unconditional and cannot be undone; files already received or downloaded are not retracted.
-   Both calls need the 0.8 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404, never a deleted message.

```dart
// Edit with the revision of the message as the user saw it.
try {
  final edited = await ConvoKit.editMessage(
    message.id,
    text: 'Can you take a look today?',
    revision: message.revision,
  );
  // edited.revision == message.revision + 1, edited.isEdited == true
} on ConvoKitException catch (error) {
  if (error.statusCode == 409 && error.code == 'REVISION_CONFLICT') {
    // Someone else changed it first: reload, show the current text, keep the
    // draft, and retry with current.revision.
    final current = await ConvoKit.getMessage(message.id);
  }
}

// Clear the caption of a message with attachments; the attachments stay.
await ConvoKit.editMessage(photo.id, text: null, revision: photo.revision);

// Delete for every member; other devices learn through onMessageDeleted.
await ConvoKit.deleteMessage(message.id);
```

### Quoted replies and jump to a message

-   `ConvoKit.sendMessage(..., replyToMessageId: quoted.id)` quotes a message of the same room and omits the key when it is null; every `Message` then carries `replyToMessageId` (null when the row is not a reply).
-   The reference is write-once — no edit changes it — and a retry with the same `clientMessageId` must repeat the same target or it fails with status 409.
-   A target in another room, or one that is gone, fails with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   Quoted text is never copied onto the reply: `ConvoKit.getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds: ids)` resolves a whole rendered page in one round trip, trimming the ids, dropping duplicates in first-seen order and splitting the distinct list into requests of 50, so you never chunk.
-   An id missing from a resolved result is the only deletion signal and is final; a failed call writes nothing and says nothing about which ids exist, so retry it on the next page.
-   `ConvoKit.getMessageContext(conversationId, messageId: id, limit: 30)` returns one window of history, newest first, centred on a message or continued from `olderCursor` or `newerCursor` — exactly one selector and a `limit` in 1..100 (default 30), checked with `ArgumentError` before any request.
-   Both cursors come back on every page and are null at that end of the room; a null `newerCursor` was only true at query time, so return to live history through the ordinary newest page.
-   Both calls need the 0.9 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404, which is never "the message is gone" — hide the affordances instead.
-   A room you are no longer an active member of answers a 404 with code `CONVERSATION_NOT_FOUND`, and a cursor the backend cannot read a 400 with code `INVALID_CURSOR`.
-   Sending a quote to an older backend is the one silent case: the message is stored without the reference, so the quote disappears when the send is confirmed.

```dart
// Quote a message of the same room; omit the argument for an ordinary send.
final reply = await ConvoKit.sendMessage(
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  text: 'Tuesday works for me.',
  replyToMessageId: quoted.id,
);

// One request for the whole rendered page, never one per row. The SDK trims the
// ids, drops duplicates and splits the distinct list into requests of 50.
final quotedIds = [
  for (final message in page)
    if (message.replyToMessageId != null) message.replyToMessageId!,
];
final previews = quotedIds.isEmpty
    ? <ReplyPreview>[]
    : await ConvoKit.getReplyPreviews(conversation.id, messageIds: quotedIds);
final previewById = {for (final preview in previews) preview.id: preview};

// An id missing from a RESOLVED result is the only 'the quoted message is gone'
// signal: keep the reply and its reference, render an unavailable placeholder,
// and never ask for that id again. A failed call says nothing about the ids.
renderQuote(reply.replyToMessageId, previewById[reply.replyToMessageId]);

// Open a quoted message that is older than the loaded history.
try {
  final context = await ConvoKit.getMessageContext(
    conversation.id,
    messageId: quoted.id,
    limit: 30,
  );
  showWindow(context.messages); // newest first, centred on the target

  // Page back toward the newest message; null means that end of the room.
  if (context.newerCursor != null) {
    final newer = await ConvoKit.getMessageContext(
      conversation.id,
      newerCursor: context.newerCursor,
    );
    showWindow(newer.messages);
  }
} on ConvoKitNotFoundException catch (error) {
  if (error.code == 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // The quoted message was deleted: keep the reply and its reference.
  }
}
```

