### Realtime streams

-   Subscribe after `connectUser` and cancel subscriptions when a screen or state owner is disposed.
-   An edit arrives on `onMessage` as an `update` carrying the new `revision` (keep the higher revision when rows meet); a deletion arrives on `onMessageDeleted` as the message ID.

```dart
final messageSub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onMessage(conversation.id)
    .listen((event) {
  // event.type is insert or update; an edit arrives as an update carrying
  // the new event.message.revision, so merge by ID and keep the higher one.
});

final deletedSub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onMessageDeleted(conversation.id)
    .listen((event) {
  // Remove event.id and keep it, so a late row cannot restore the message.
});

final typingSub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onTyping(conversation.id)
    .listen((event) {
  // event.userId and event.isTyping
});

final readSub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onReadReceipt(conversation.id)
    .listen((event) {
  // event.userId, event.readAt and event.readPosition
});
```

### Presence, typing, and reads

-   Broadcast UI state through SDK helpers and consume the matching realtime streams.
-   A read names the newest rendered message; omit `throughMessageId` only when nothing is rendered.
-   Add the `privateStateVersion` captured when the room opened to also clear your own unread marker while it is still current (see Mark unread).

```dart
final presenceSub = ConvoKit.realtime
    .onPresence(ConvoKit.clientId)
    .listen((event) {
  // event.userId, event.isOnline, event.lastSeenAt
});

await ConvoKit.updatePresence(isOnline: true);
await ConvoKit.sendTyping(
  conversationId: conversation.id,
  isTyping: true,
);

// Name the newest message the user has actually seen.
await ConvoKit.markConversationRead(
  conversation.id,
  throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
);
```

### Compute read receipts

Participants and read events carry `readPosition` beside the acknowledgement time. Use `readThrough` instead of comparing timestamps; it falls back to `lastReadAt` only for a participant without a position.

```dart
final participant = conversation.participants
    .firstWhere((p) => p.appUserId == readerId);

// The position decides by conversation order when present;
// lastReadAt is the fallback for a participant without one.
final seen = readThrough(
  message,
  readPosition: participant.readPosition,
  lastReadAt: participant.lastReadAt,
);

ConvoKit.realtime.onReadReceipt(conversation.id).listen((event) {
  // event.readPosition is the newest message event.userId has read.
  final seenNow = readThrough(
    message,
    readPosition: event.readPosition,
    lastReadAt: event.readAt,
  );
});
```

### Session

Configure the SDK once, connect an app user, and clean up realtime subscriptions on sign out.

`ConvoKit.configure(...)`

Sets the public client ID and token provider; the managed API endpoint is automatic.

`ConvoKit.connectUser(appUserId)`

Fetches a scoped user token and initializes realtime auth.

`ConvoKit.disconnectUser()`

Disposes active realtime channels for the current user.

`ConvoKit.currentUserId`

Returns the connected app user ID.

### Conversations

Create and manage conversation membership and metadata from the Flutter client.

`ConvoKit.getConversations(...)`

Lists active conversations in creation order, with offset pagination and archived filtering.

`ConvoKit.listInbox({int limit = 30, String? cursor, bool archived = false})`

Lists the inbox newest activity first with a preview, unread count and the caller’s read state per entry, paged by an opaque cursor. A limit outside 1..100 throws ArgumentError before any request.

`ConvoKit.getConversation(id)`

Fetches one conversation the current user participates in, with their own membership (role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion); capture privateStateVersion when the room opens.

`ConvoKit.createConversation(...)`

Creates a conversation with app user participants.

`ConvoKit.updateConversationTitle(...)`

Updates or clears a conversation title.

`ConvoKit.archiveConversation(id)`

Archives a conversation for the current user.

`ConvoKit.unarchiveConversation(id)`

Restores an archived conversation.

`ConvoKit.leaveConversation(id)`

Removes the current user from a conversation.

`ConvoKit.markConversationRead(id, {String? throughMessageId, int? privateStateVersion})`

Records the read position through the newest rendered message; omit the target to read through the newest message on the server. Positions never move backward. privateStateVersion, the version captured at open, also clears your unread marker while it is still current; omit it to leave the marker alone.

`ConvoKit.markConversationUnread(String conversationId)`

Marks the room unread for the current user only and returns a ConversationPrivateState (conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion). Every call advances the version; the count is untouched.

`ConvoKit.clearConversationUnread(String conversationId, {int? ifVersion})`

Removes your unread marker without acknowledging a message, only while it still has ifVersion when given. Returns a ClearUnreadResult whose cleared is true or false (a no-op is not an error) with the current private state.

### Messages and media

Send text, attach images or files, and paginate message history.

`ConvoKit.sendMessage(...)`

Sends text and optional media to a conversation. replyToMessageId quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when null; the reference is write-once, so a retry with the same clientMessageId must repeat it, and a target that is gone or in another room throws a ConvoKitNotFoundException with code MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`ConvoKit.getMessages(...)`

Loads messages for a conversation with limit and offset; every Message carries revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit by its author or your server) and replyToMessageId when the row quotes another message.

`ConvoKit.getMessage(String id)`

Loads one message the current user can see, with its attachments and current revision; the reload after a 409 conflict.

`ConvoKit.editMessage(String messageId, {required String? text, required int revision})`

Author edit: replaces the text of one of the current user’s own messages, or clears the caption of a message with attachments with a null text, and returns the updated Message (revision + 1, attachments unchanged). revision is the row’s revision as the user saw it; a stale one throws a ConvoKitValidationException with statusCode 409 and code REVISION\_CONFLICT, so reload with getMessage and retry. Both keys are always sent; a revision outside 0..2147483647 throws ArgumentError before any request.

`ConvoKit.deleteMessage(String messageId)`

Author delete: removes one of the current user’s own messages for every member. Unconditional (no revision) and cannot be undone; other devices learn through onMessageDeleted. A message that is already gone throws a ConvoKitNotFoundException with code MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`ConvoKit.getReplyPreviews(String conversationId, {required List<String> messageIds})`

Resolves the quoted messages a rendered page points at in one round trip, never one request per row. The ids are trimmed and de-duplicated in first-seen order and the distinct list is split into requests of 50, merged in that order; an empty list, a blank id or an id over 64 characters throws ArgumentError before any request. Ids that do not exist, were deleted or belong to another room are simply absent from a returned result — the only deletion signal — while a failed call says nothing about which ids exist.

`ConvoKit.getMessageContext(String conversationId, {String? messageId, String? olderCursor, String? newerCursor, int limit = 30})`

Returns one window of a room’s history as a MessageContextPage (messages newest first, olderCursor and newerCursor always present and null at that end of the room). Exactly one of messageId, olderCursor and newerCursor, and a limit in 1..100, both checked with ArgumentError before any request. A centred window always contains its target; an unknown, deleted or foreign messageId throws a ConvoKitNotFoundException with code MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND and an unreadable cursor a ConvoKitValidationException with code INVALID\_CURSOR.

`ConvoKit.uploadMessageMedia(...)`

Uploads an image or file and returns the URL to include in a message.

`ConvoKit.uploadUserAvatar(...)`

Uploads and assigns a user avatar.

`ConvoKit.uploadConversationImage(...)`

Uploads and assigns a conversation image.

`ConvoKit.deleteUserAvatar(...)`

Clears a user avatar.

`ConvoKit.deleteConversationImage(...)`

Clears a conversation image.

### Realtime

Subscribe to realtime streams after connecting the user.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onMessage(id)`

Streams inserted and updated messages for a conversation as events with type and message; an edit arrives as an update carrying the new revision, so merge by ID and keep the higher revision.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onMessageDeleted(id)`

Streams the IDs of deleted messages for a conversation; remove the row and keep the ID so a late response cannot restore it.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onTyping(id)`

Streams typing indicator events.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onReadReceipt(id)`

Streams read receipt events carrying the reader, acknowledgement time, and read position.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onPresence(clientId)`

Streams online and last-seen events for the app.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onInboxChanged(clientId)`

Signals when your custom inbox should reload after membership, metadata, profile or deletion changes, including after reconnecting.

`ConvoKit.realtime.onInboxActivity(clientId)`

Empty Stream<void> after a message is sent or edited, a read position advances or your own unread marker changes anywhere in the app. Never raised on connection; throttle the reload it triggers.

`ConvoKit.updatePresence(...)`

Broadcasts the current user online or offline.

`ConvoKit.sendTyping(...)`

Broadcasts typing state to other participants.

### Exported models and events

Import from `package:convokit_flutter/convokit_flutter.dart` to use these types in screens, repositories, and state managers.

`Conversation`id, title, imageUrl, appId, displayTitle, description, participants, createdAt, updatedAt; membership (your own row) on getConversation results only

`ConversationMembership`role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt (DateTime?), privateStateVersion; never part of participants or inbox entries

`Message`id, conversationId, senderId, clientMessageId, text, media, createdAt, updatedAt, revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit) and the derived isEdited (revision > 0), replyToMessageId (the quoted message when the row is a reply, null otherwise); copyWith rebuilds a row without dropping a field

`ReplyPreview`id, conversationId, senderId, text (first 500 characters, null when the quoted message has none), textTruncated, createdAt, revision, mediaCount; resolved by getReplyPreviews and never embedded in a Message

`MessageContextPage`messages (newest first) plus olderCursor and newerCursor, each null when the window reached that end of the room

`Participant`id, appUserId, name, imageUrl, role, lastReadAt, readPosition

`ReadPosition`messageId, createdAt, covers(message); readThrough(message, readPosition:, lastReadAt:) applies the shared rule

`InboxSummary`latestMessage (Message?, at most its first 4 media), unreadCount, unreadCountCapped, readPosition, lastReadAt, isUnread, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion, activityAt

`InboxEntry`conversation (participants limited to 10) and summary, with the summary fields also exposed directly

`InboxPage`entries and nextCursor (String?, null on the last page)

`ConversationPrivateState / ClearUnreadResult`conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion; ClearUnreadResult adds cleared

`MessageEvent / MessageDeletedEvent`type (insert or update) and message; id and conversationId

`TypingEvent`userId, isTyping

`ReadEvent`userId, readAt, readPosition

`PresenceEvent`userId, isOnline, lastSeenAt

### Error handling

-   REST helpers throw `ConvoKitException` when the backend returns a non-success response.
-   `statusCode` carries the HTTP status and `code` the backend error code when the body includes one, such as `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` for a read whose target is not a message in that conversation, or `INVALID_CURSOR` (a `ConvoKitValidationException` with status 400) for an inbox cursor ConvoKit did not issue.
-   A `listInbox` limit outside 1..100, or a `privateStateVersion`, `ifVersion` or `revision` outside 0..2147483647, throws `ArgumentError` before any request; against an older backend the mark and clear calls fail with status 404.
-   `editMessage` with a stale `revision` throws a `ConvoKitValidationException` with `statusCode` 409 and `code` `REVISION_CONFLICT` (nothing was written: reload the row with `getMessage` and retry); another member's message or a `READ` role throws a 403 `ConvoKitAuthException`; a message the caller cannot see, or one already deleted, throws a `ConvoKitNotFoundException` with `code` `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` on `editMessage`, `deleteMessage` and `getMessage` alike.
-   Against an older backend the author calls fail with status 404 and no `code`, which is never a deleted message.

```dart
try {
  await ConvoKit.markConversationRead(
    conversation.id,
    throughMessageId: newestRenderedMessage.id,
  );
} on ConvoKitException catch (error) {
  if (error.code == 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // Acknowledge the next newest rendered message instead.
  } else {
    // Show retry UI or log error.message.
  }
}

try {
  await ConvoKit.editMessage(message.id, text: draft, revision: message.revision);
} on ConvoKitException catch (error) {
  if (error.statusCode == 409 && error.code == 'REVISION_CONFLICT') {
    // Stale revision: reload the message, show it, and retry with its revision.
  } else if (error.code == 'MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND') {
    // Deleted or no longer accessible: remove the row.
  }
}
```

### Session lifecycle

Connect the user before creating subscriptions or SDK-backed UI. Your token provider must fetch fresh tokens from your authenticated backend.

On sign-out or account change, dispose the current UI controllers and subscriptions, then disconnect the client. Create a new adapter or controller after the next successful login, even when signing back in as the same user.

See [authentication](https://convokit.app/docs/auth) for the token flow and [messaging behavior](https://convokit.app/docs/messaging) for read receipts, retries, timestamps, and what the SDK-backed UI handles automatically.

Swift SDK

# Build native iOS chat with async Swift APIs and realtime streams.

The ConvoKit Swift SDK is a client-only binary package for iOS 15+. It covers conversations, structured media, read receipts, typing, presence, and protected attachments while keeping your client secret on your backend.

Published`ConvoKit 0.10.1`

[Swift package](https://github.com/ConvoKitApp/ConvoKit-Swift-Package) [Public example](https://github.com/ConvoKitApp/ConvoKit-Swift-UI-Examples) [SwiftUI components](https://convokit.app/docs/swift-ui)

### Install with Swift Package Manager

Add the ConvoKit package URL to your app. No registry login or GitHub token is required. Use the example to try a complete chat integration.

### Install with Swift Package Manager

Select the ConvoKit product for the app target.

```swift
dependencies: [
    .package(
        url: "https://github.com/ConvoKitApp/ConvoKit-Swift-Package",
        exact: "0.10.1"
    )
]

// Add the ConvoKit product to your iOS app target.
```

### Configure and connect

Inject the host app's token exchange as an async closure. The SDK uses https://api.convokit.app automatically.

```swift
let convoKit = try ConvoKitClient(
    clientId: "your-public-client-id"
) { appUserId in
    // Call your authenticated backend and return only its scoped user token.
    try await appBackend.issueConvoKitToken(for: appUserId)
}

try await convoKit.connectUser(currentUser.id)
```

### The client secret never belongs in an iOS app

Ship only the public client ID. Your authenticated backend stores the secret, issues a scoped user token, and decides whether a user may join a room.

### Conversations and messages

-   Every network operation uses Swift concurrency.
-   A read names the newest rendered message; `markConversationRead(_:)` without a target reads through the newest message on the server, and positions never move backward.
-   Add the `privateStateVersion` captured when the room opened to also clear your own unread marker while it is still current (see Mark unread).

```swift
let room = try await convoKit.createConversation(.init(
    participants: [currentUser.id, teammate.id],
    title: "Launch room",
    description: "Release coordination"
))

let sent = try await convoKit.sendMessage(.init(
    conversationId: room.id,
    text: "The release is ready."
))

let history = try await convoKit.getMessages(
    conversationId: room.id,
    limit: 30
)

// Name the newest message the user has actually seen.
try await convoKit.markConversationRead(
    room.id,
    throughMessageId: newestRendered.id
)
```

### Inbox previews and unread counts

-   `listInbox(limit:cursor:archived:)` returns an `InboxPage` of rooms newest activity first (latest surviving message, then creation time).
-   Each `InboxEntry` carries the `conversation` beside `latestMessage`, `unreadCount`, `unreadCountCapped`, your `readPosition`, `lastReadAt` and `activityAt`.
-   `unreadCount` counts messages from other users after your read position and is exact up to 1,000; a capped count is a lower bound.
-   `limit` defaults to 30 and must be 1...100.

```swift
let page = try await convoKit.listInbox(limit: 30)

for entry in page.entries {
    // A count (or a capped count) is a number; a marker alone is a dot, never an invented count.
    let badge: String? = entry.unreadCountCapped || entry.unreadCount > 99 ? "99+"
        : entry.unreadCount > 0 ? String(entry.unreadCount) : nil
    let dot = entry.isUnread && entry.unreadCount == 0 && !entry.unreadCountCapped
    renderRow(entry.conversation.displayTitle, entry.latestMessage?.text, badge, dot, entry.activityAt)
}

// Walk older rooms with the opaque cursor until it is nil.
if let cursor = page.nextCursor {
    let older = try await convoKit.listInbox(cursor: cursor)
}

// Refetch on both app-wide signals; throttle the activity one.
let structuralTask = Task {
    do {
        for try await _ in realtime.onInboxChanged(appId: convoKit.clientId) {
            await viewModel.reloadInbox()
        }
    } catch { await viewModel.showError(error) }
}
let activityTask = Task {
    do {
        for try await _ in realtime.onInboxActivity(appId: convoKit.clientId) {
            await viewModel.scheduleInboxReload()
        }
    } catch { await viewModel.showError(error) }
}
```

### Mark unread

-   `markConversationUnread(_:)` flags a room for the current user only: other members, webhooks and read events never see the marker, and `unreadCount` is untouched.
-   `InboxSummary` carries `isUnread` (true for a count, a capped count or the marker), `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion`; render a numberless dot when the count is 0, never an invented count.
-   Capture `membership?.privateStateVersion` from `getConversation` once per open and send it through `markConversationRead(_:throughMessageId:privateStateVersion:)` with every acknowledgement of that open, so a mark made later survives a delayed read; `clearConversationUnread(_:ifVersion:)` clears an empty room the same way.
-   Marker changes reach your other devices through `onInboxActivity(appId:)`; against an older backend `membership` is nil and the mark and clear calls fail with status 404.

```swift
// Flag the room for the current user only; other members never see the marker.
let state = try await convoKit.markConversationUnread(room.id)
// state.unreadMarkedAt, state.privateStateVersion

// Capture the version once, when the room opens (nil on an older backend).
let opened = try await convoKit.getConversation(room.id).membership?.privateStateVersion

// Every acknowledgement of that open carries it: the marker clears only while
// the version is still current, so a mark made after the open survives.
try await convoKit.markConversationRead(
    room.id,
    throughMessageId: newestRendered.id,
    privateStateVersion: opened
)

// An empty room has nothing to acknowledge: clear the marker conditionally instead.
let result = try await convoKit.clearConversationUnread(room.id, ifVersion: opened)
// result.cleared is false, not an error, when nothing was marked or the version moved on.
```

### Edit and delete your own messages

-   `editMessage(_:text:revision:)` and `deleteMessage(_:)` are the author operations: only the sender may call them, while still an active READ\_WRITE member (other members' messages and a READ role fail with status 403 and `HTTP_ERROR`).
-   Every `Message` carries `revision`, 0 when sent and +1 on every edit by its author or by your server; `isEdited` (`revision > 0`) is the only edited signal, never `updatedAt`.
-   Send the row's `revision` with every edit: a stale one fails with status 409 and code `REVISION_CONFLICT` and nothing is written, so reload with `getMessage`, show the current text and retry with its revision.
-   `text: nil` clears the caption of a message with attachments; attachments are never changed by an edit, and a text-only message cannot be emptied.
-   Deleting is unconditional and cannot be undone; files already received or downloaded are not retracted.
-   Both calls need the 0.8 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), never a deleted message.
-   `revision` has a memberwise default of 0, so existing `Message` literals keep compiling.

```swift
// Edit with the revision of the message as the user saw it.
do {
    let edited = try await convoKit.editMessage(
        message.id,
        text: "Can you take a look today?",
        revision: message.revision
    )
    _ = edited.isEdited // true: the revision moved from message.revision to message.revision + 1
} catch let error as ConvoKitError where error.code == "REVISION_CONFLICT" {
    // Someone else changed it first: reload, show the current text, keep the
    // draft, and retry with current.revision.
    let current = try await convoKit.getMessage(message.id)
}

// Clear the caption of a message with attachments; the attachments stay.
_ = try await convoKit.editMessage(photo.id, text: nil, revision: photo.revision)

// Delete for every member; other devices learn through onMessageDeleted.
try await convoKit.deleteMessage(message.id)
```

### Quoted replies and jump to a message

-   `SendMessageInput.replyToMessageId` quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when nil; every `Message` then carries `replyToMessageId` (nil when the row is not a reply, with a memberwise default so existing literals keep compiling).
-   The reference is write-once — no edit changes it — and a retry with the same `clientMessageId` must repeat the same target or it fails with status 409.
-   A target in another room, or one that is gone, fails with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   Quoted text is never copied onto the reply: `getReplyPreviews(conversationId:messageIds:)` resolves a whole rendered page in one round trip, trimming the ids, dropping duplicates in first-seen order and splitting the distinct list into requests of 50, so you never chunk.
-   An id missing from a resolved result is the only deletion signal and is final; a failed call writes nothing and says nothing about which ids exist, so retry it on the next page.
-   `getMessageContext(conversationId:messageId:olderCursor:newerCursor:limit:)` returns one window of history, newest first, centred on a message or continued from a cursor — exactly one selector and a `limit` in 1...100 (default 30), `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request.
-   Both cursors come back on every page and are nil at that end of the room; a nil `newerCursor` was only true at query time, so return to live history through the ordinary newest page.
-   Both calls need the 0.9 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), which is never "the message is gone" — hide the affordances instead.
-   A room you are no longer an active member of answers a 404 with code `CONVERSATION_NOT_FOUND`, and a cursor the backend cannot read a 400 with code `INVALID_CURSOR`.
-   Sending a quote to an older backend is the one silent case: the message is stored without the reference, so the quote disappears when the send is confirmed.

```swift
// Quote a message of the same room; omit the field for an ordinary send.
let reply = try await convoKit.sendMessage(.init(
    conversationId: room.id,
    text: "Tuesday works for me.",
    replyToMessageId: quoted.id
))

// One request for the whole rendered page, never one per row. The SDK trims the
// ids, drops duplicates and splits the distinct list into requests of 50.
let quotedIds = page.compactMap(\.replyToMessageId)
let previews = quotedIds.isEmpty
    ? []
    : try await convoKit.getReplyPreviews(conversationId: room.id, messageIds: quotedIds)
let previewById = Dictionary(uniqueKeysWithValues: previews.map { ($0.id, $0) })

// An id missing from a RESOLVED result is the only "the quoted message is gone"
// signal: keep the reply and its reference, render an unavailable placeholder,
// and never ask for that id again. A failed call says nothing about the ids.
renderQuote(reply.replyToMessageId, previewById[reply.replyToMessageId ?? ""])

// Open a quoted message that is older than the loaded history.
do {
    let context = try await convoKit.getMessageContext(
        conversationId: room.id,
        messageId: quoted.id,
        limit: 30
    )
    showWindow(context.messages) // newest first, centred on the target

    // Page back toward the newest message; nil means that end of the room.
    if let cursor = context.newerCursor {
        let newer = try await convoKit.getMessageContext(
            conversationId: room.id,
            newerCursor: cursor
        )
        showWindow(newer.messages)
    }
} catch let error as ConvoKitError where error.code == "MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND" {
    // The quoted message was deleted: keep the reply and its reference.
}
```

