### Inbox previews and unread counts

-   `listInbox` returns an `InboxPage` of rooms newest activity first (latest surviving message, then creation time).
-   Each `InboxEntry` carries the `conversation` beside `latestMessage`, `unreadCount`, `unreadCountCapped`, your `readPosition`, `lastReadAt` and `activityAt`.
-   `unreadCount` counts messages from other users after your read position and is exact up to 1,000; a capped count is a lower bound.
-   `limit` defaults to 30 and must be 1..100; `cursor` is omitted when null.

```kotlin
val page = convoKit.listInbox(limit = 30)

page.entries.forEach { entry ->
    // A count (or a capped count) is a number; a marker alone is a dot, never an invented count.
    val badge = when {
        entry.unreadCountCapped || entry.unreadCount > 99 -> "99+"
        entry.unreadCount > 0 -> entry.unreadCount.toString()
        else -> null
    }
    val dot = entry.isUnread && entry.unreadCount == 0 && !entry.unreadCountCapped
    renderRow(entry.conversation.displayTitle, entry.latestMessage?.text, badge, dot, entry.activityAt)
}

// Walk older rooms with the opaque cursor until it is null.
val older = page.nextCursor?.let { convoKit.listInbox(cursor = it) }

// Refetch on both app-wide signals; throttle the activity one.
viewModelScope.launch {
    convoKit.realtime.onInboxChanged(convoKit.clientId).collect { reloadInbox() }
}
viewModelScope.launch {
    convoKit.realtime.onInboxActivity(convoKit.clientId).collect { scheduleReload() }
}
```

### Mark unread

-   `markConversationUnread` flags a room for the connected user only: other members, webhooks and read events never see the marker, and `unreadCount` is untouched.
-   `InboxSummary` carries `isUnread` (true for a count, a capped count or the marker), `unreadMarkedAt` and `privateStateVersion`; render a numberless dot when the count is 0, never an invented count.
-   Capture `membership?.privateStateVersion` from `getConversation` once per open and send it through the three-argument `markConversationRead` with every acknowledgement of that open, so a mark made later survives a delayed read; `clearConversationUnread` with `ifVersion` clears an empty room the same way.
-   Marker changes reach your other devices through `onInboxActivity`; against an older backend `membership` is null and the mark and clear calls fail with status 404.

```kotlin
// Flag the room for the current user only; other members never see the marker.
val state = convoKit.markConversationUnread(room.id)
// state.unreadMarkedAt, state.privateStateVersion

// Capture the version once, when the room opens (null on an older backend).
val opened = convoKit.getConversation(room.id).membership?.privateStateVersion

// Every acknowledgement of that open carries it: the marker clears only while
// the version is still current, so a mark made after the open survives.
convoKit.markConversationRead(room.id, newestRendered.id, opened)

// An empty room has nothing to acknowledge: clear the marker conditionally instead.
val result = convoKit.clearConversationUnread(room.id, ifVersion = opened)
// result.cleared is false, not an error, when nothing was marked or the version moved on.
```

