Send text and paginate room history.

```kotlin
val sent = convoKit.sendMessage(
    SendMessageInput(
        conversationId = room.id,
        text = "The release is ready.",
    ),
)

val history = convoKit.getMessages(room.id, limit = 20, offset = 0)
val sameMessage = convoKit.getMessage(sent.id)
```

### Edit and delete your own messages

-   `editMessage(messageId, text, revision)` and `deleteMessage(messageId)` are the author operations: only the sender may call them, while still an active READ\_WRITE member (other members' messages and a READ role fail with status 403 and `HTTP_ERROR`).
-   Every `Message` carries `revision`, 0 when sent and +1 on every edit by its author or by your server; `isEdited` (`revision > 0`) is the only edited signal, never `updatedAt`.
-   Send the row's `revision` with every edit: a stale one fails with status 409 and code `REVISION_CONFLICT` and nothing is written, so reload with `getMessage`, show the current text and retry with its revision.
-   A null `text` clears the caption of a message with attachments; attachments are never changed by an edit, and a text-only message cannot be emptied.
-   Deleting is unconditional and cannot be undone; files already received or downloaded are not retracted.
-   Both calls need the 0.8 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), never a deleted message.
-   `revision` is a trailing defaulted field of the `Message` data class, so named-argument literals keep compiling while `copy()` and `componentN()` changed.

```kotlin
// Edit with the revision of the message as the user saw it.
try {
    val edited = convoKit.editMessage(message.id, "Can you take another look?", revision = message.revision)
    if (edited.isEdited) { /* render "Edited" beside the time */ }
} catch (error: ConvoKitException) {
    if (error.code != "REVISION_CONFLICT") throw error
    // Someone else changed it first: reload, show the current text, keep the
    // draft, and retry with current.revision.
    val current = convoKit.getMessage(message.id)
}

// Clear the caption of a message with attachments; the attachments stay.
convoKit.editMessage(photo.id, text = null, revision = photo.revision)

// Delete for every member; other devices learn through onMessageDeleted.
convoKit.deleteMessage(message.id)
```

### Quoted replies and jump to a message

-   `SendMessageInput.replyToMessageId` quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when null; every `Message` then carries `replyToMessageId` (null when the row is not a reply, and a trailing defaulted field so named-argument literals keep compiling).
-   The reference is write-once — no edit changes it — and a retry with the same `clientMessageId` must repeat the same target or it fails with status 409.
-   A target in another room, or one that is gone, fails with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`.
-   Quoted text is never copied onto the reply: `getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)` resolves a whole rendered page in one round trip, trimming the ids, dropping duplicates in first-seen order and splitting the distinct list into requests of 50, so you never chunk.
-   An id missing from a resolved result is the only deletion signal and is final; a failed call writes nothing and says nothing about which ids exist, so retry it on the next page.
-   `getMessageContext(conversationId, messageId, olderCursor, newerCursor, limit = 30)` returns one window of history, newest first, centred on a message or continued from a cursor — exactly one selector and a `limit` in 1..100 (default 30), both `INVALID_ARGUMENT` before any request.
-   Both cursors come back on every page and are null at that end of the room; a null `newerCursor` was only true at query time, so return to live history through the ordinary newest page.
-   Both calls need the 0.9 backend: an older backend answers an uncoded 404 (`HTTP_ERROR`), which is never "the message is gone" — hide the affordances instead.
-   A room you are no longer an active member of answers a 404 with code `CONVERSATION_NOT_FOUND`, and a cursor the backend cannot read a 400 with code `INVALID_CURSOR`.
-   Sending a quote to an older backend is the one silent case: the message is stored without the reference, so the quote disappears when the send is confirmed.

```kotlin
// Quote a message of the same room; omit the field for an ordinary send.
val reply = convoKit.sendMessage(
    SendMessageInput(
        conversationId = room.id,
        text = "Tuesday works for me.",
        replyToMessageId = quoted.id,
    ),
)

// One request for the whole rendered page, never one per row. The SDK trims the
// ids, drops duplicates and splits the distinct list into requests of 50.
val quotedIds = page.mapNotNull { it.replyToMessageId }
val previews = if (quotedIds.isEmpty()) emptyList()
    else convoKit.getReplyPreviews(room.id, quotedIds)
val previewById = previews.associateBy { it.id }

// An id missing from a RESOLVED result is the only "the quoted message is gone"
// signal: keep the reply and its reference, render an unavailable placeholder,
// and never ask for that id again. A failed call says nothing about the ids.
renderQuote(reply.replyToMessageId, previewById[reply.replyToMessageId])

// Open a quoted message that is older than the loaded history.
try {
    val context = convoKit.getMessageContext(room.id, messageId = quoted.id, limit = 50)
    showWindow(context.messages) // newest first, centred on the target

    // Page back toward the newest message; null means that end of the room.
    context.newerCursor?.let { cursor ->
        showWindow(convoKit.getMessageContext(room.id, newerCursor = cursor).messages)
    }
} catch (error: ConvoKitException) {
    if (error.code != "MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND") throw error
    // The quoted message was deleted: keep the reply and its reference.
}
```

