### Realtime Flow

Collect typed streams from lifecycle-owned coroutines. An edit arrives on `onMessage` as an UPDATE carrying the new `revision` (keep the higher revision when rows meet); a deletion arrives on `onMessageDeleted` as the message ID.

```kotlin
viewModelScope.launch {
    // INSERT or UPDATE: an edit arrives as an UPDATE carrying the new
    // event.message.revision, so merge by ID and keep the higher revision.
    convoKit.realtime.onMessage(room.id).collect { event -> upsertMessage(event.message) }
}

viewModelScope.launch {
    // Remove the ID and keep it, so a late row cannot restore the message.
    convoKit.realtime.onMessageDeleted(room.id).collect { event -> removeMessage(event.id) }
}

viewModelScope.launch {
    convoKit.realtime.onTyping(room.id).collect { event ->
        updateTyping(event.userId, event.isTyping)
    }
}

viewModelScope.launch {
    convoKit.realtime.onReadReceipt(room.id).collect { event ->
        updateReadState(event.userId, event.readPosition, event.readAt)
    }
}

viewModelScope.launch {
    convoKit.realtime.onPresence(convoKit.clientId).collect(::updatePresence)
}
```

### Read receipts

Participants and read events carry `readPosition` beside the acknowledgement time. Resolve readers with `readThrough` instead of comparing timestamps, and keep the newest position per user from live events.

```kotlin
// Durable state returned with every conversation. The position decides by
// conversation order when present; lastReadAt is the fallback without one.
val readers = room.participants.filter { participant ->
    participant.appUserId != message.senderId &&
        readThrough(participant.readPosition, participant.lastReadAt, message)
}

// Then merge live receipt events, keeping the newest position per user.
convoKit.realtime.onReadReceipt(room.id).collect { event ->
    readAtByUserId[event.userId] = event.readAt
    val incoming = event.readPosition ?: return@collect
    val current = readPositionByUserId[event.userId]
    if (current == null ||
        compareValuesBy(incoming, current, { it.createdAt }, { it.messageId }) > 0
    ) {
        readPositionByUserId[event.userId] = incoming
    }
}
```

### Typing, presence, and cleanup

-   Publish ephemeral state and dispose on sign out.
-   A read names the newest rendered message; a target that is no longer in the conversation fails with code `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND`, so acknowledge the next newest rendered message instead.
-   Pass the `privateStateVersion` captured when the room opened as the third argument to also clear your own unread marker while it is still current (see Mark unread).
-   Argument checks (a negative `privateStateVersion`, `ifVersion` or `revision`) fail before any request with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`; backend codes worth branching on are `MESSAGE_NOT_FOUND` (404), `REVISION_CONFLICT` (409, `editMessage`) and `INVALID_CURSOR` (400), and responses without a JSON code carry `HTTP_ERROR` with the HTTP status.

```kotlin
convoKit.sendTyping(room.id, isTyping = true)
// Name the newest message the user has actually seen.
convoKit.markConversationRead(room.id, throughMessageId = newestRendered.id)
convoKit.updatePresence(isOnline = true)

// On host-user sign out:
convoKit.disconnectUser()
```

### Joining a room by ID

Joining is deliberately not an unrestricted client SDK method. Your backend validates policy and adds membership before Android loads the room. The public example includes this complete flow.

```typescript
// Server: enforce your product's room policy, then add membership.
await admin.addConversationMember(roomId, {
  appUserId: request.user.id,
  role: 'READ_WRITE',
})

// Android: call that join endpoint before loading the room.
yourApi.joinRoom(roomId)
val room = convoKit.getConversation(roomId)
```

### Session and users

`connectUser / disconnectUser`

Starts or disposes the user session and shared realtime socket.

`connected / currentUserId`

Reports the active app-user session.

`authHeaders / lastUserToken`

Exposes authenticated context for advanced REST integrations.

`getUsers / getUser`

Lists app users with pagination or fetches one by ID.

### Conversations

`getConversations / getConversation`

Lists active or archived rooms in creation order and loads one authorized room. getConversation also fills your own membership (role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion); capture privateStateVersion when the room opens.

`listInbox(limit = 30, cursor = null, archived = false)`

Lists the inbox newest activity first with a preview, unread count and read state per entry, paged by an opaque cursor. A limit outside 1..100 fails before any request with code INVALID\_ARGUMENT.

`createConversation`

Creates a room with participants and optional metadata.

`updateConversationTitle`

Changes or clears the participant-facing title.

`archiveConversation / unarchiveConversation`

Controls the connected user’s archived state.

`leaveConversation`

Removes the current user from a room.

`markConversationRead(conversationId, throughMessageId, privateStateVersion)`

Records the read position through the newest rendered message; the one-argument overload reads through the newest message on the server. Positions never move backward. privateStateVersion, the version captured at open, also clears your unread marker while it is still current; the one- and two-argument overloads send none and leave the marker alone.

`markConversationUnread(conversationId)`

Marks the room unread for the connected user only and returns a ConversationPrivateState (conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion). Every call advances the version; the count is untouched.

`clearConversationUnread(conversationId, ifVersion = null)`

Removes your unread marker without acknowledging a message, only while it still has ifVersion when given. Returns a ClearUnreadResult whose cleared is true or false (a no-op is not an error) with the current private state.

`ReadPosition.covers / readThrough`

Decides whether a message is read: the position by conversation order when present, otherwise lastReadAt.

### Messages and media

`getMessages / getMessage`

Loads paginated history or one message; every Message carries revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit by its author or your server) and isEdited, plus replyToMessageId when the row quotes another message.

`sendMessage`

Sends text plus image, file, location, or contact media. SendMessageInput.replyToMessageId quotes a message of the same room and is omitted from the request when null; the reference is write-once, so a retry with the same clientMessageId must repeat it, and a target that is gone or in another room fails with MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`editMessage(messageId, text, revision)`

Author edit: replaces the text of one of the connected user’s own messages, or clears the caption of a message with attachments with a null text, and returns the updated Message (revision + 1, attachments unchanged). revision is the row’s revision as the user saw it; a stale one fails with status 409 and code REVISION\_CONFLICT, so reload with getMessage and retry. Both keys are always sent; a negative revision fails before any request with INVALID\_ARGUMENT.

`deleteMessage(messageId)`

Author delete: removes one of the connected user’s own messages for every member. Unconditional (no revision) and cannot be undone; other devices learn through realtime.onMessageDeleted. A message that is already gone fails with code MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND.

`getReplyPreviews(conversationId, messageIds)`

Resolves the quoted messages a rendered page points at in one round trip, never one request per row. The ids are trimmed and de-duplicated in first-seen order and the distinct list is split into requests of 50, merged in that order; an empty list, a blank id or an id over 64 characters fails before any request with INVALID\_ARGUMENT. Ids that do not exist, were deleted or belong to another room are simply absent from the result — the only deletion signal — while a failed call says nothing about which ids exist.

`getMessageContext(conversationId, messageId, olderCursor, newerCursor, limit = 30)`

Returns one window of a room’s history as a MessageContextPage (messages newest first, olderCursor and newerCursor always present and null at that end of the room). Exactly one of messageId, olderCursor and newerCursor, and a limit in 1..100, both checked with INVALID\_ARGUMENT before any request. A centred window always contains its target; an unknown, deleted or foreign messageId fails with MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND and an unreadable cursor with INVALID\_CURSOR.

`uploadMessageMedia`

Uploads and verifies an attachment before returning its URL.

`uploadUserAvatar / deleteUserAvatar`

Assigns or clears an app-user avatar.

`uploadConversationImage / deleteConversationImage`

Assigns or clears a room image.

`downloadMedia`

Downloads protected media through the authenticated proxy.

### Realtime state

`realtime.onMessage`

Returns a Flow<MessageEvent> of inserted and updated messages for one room; an edit arrives as an UPDATE carrying the new revision, so merge by ID and keep the higher revision.

`realtime.onMessageDeleted`

Returns a Flow<MessageDeletedEvent> with the IDs of deleted messages for one room; remove the row and keep the ID so a late response cannot restore it.

`realtime.onTyping`

Returns a Flow of typing state.

`realtime.onReadReceipt`

Returns a Flow of live read events with the reader, acknowledgement time, and read position.

`realtime.onPresence`

Returns a Flow of online and last-seen state.

`realtime.onInboxChanged`

Signals when your custom inbox should reload after membership, metadata, profile or deletion changes, including after reconnecting.

`realtime.onInboxActivity`

Returns a Flow<Unit> that emits after a message is sent or edited, a read position advances or your own unread marker changes anywhere in the app. Never raised on connection; throttle the reload it triggers.

`realtime.connectionStatus / errors`

Exposes socket status and non-fatal channel errors.

`sendTyping / updatePresence`

Publishes the current user’s ephemeral state.

### Typed models

Public values use kotlinx-datetime and kotlinx-serialization JSON types.

`AppUser`ID, app ID, name, image, last seen, and timestamps

`Conversation`Metadata and typed participants with role, lastReadAt, and readPosition; a trailing membership (your own row, null except on getConversation)

`ConversationMembership`role, lastReadAt, readPosition, unreadMarkedAt (Instant?), privateStateVersion; never part of participants or inbox entries

`ReadPosition`messageId, createdAt, and covers(message); readThrough(readPosition, lastReadAt, message) applies the shared rule

`Message`Sender, clientMessageId, text, structured media, timestamps, and a trailing revision (0 when sent, +1 per edit; defaulted, so named-argument literals keep compiling) with the derived isEdited (revision > 0), then a trailing replyToMessageId (the quoted message when the row is a reply, null otherwise; also defaulted)

`ReplyPreview`id, conversationId, senderId, text (first 500 characters, null when the quoted message has none), textTruncated, createdAt, revision, mediaCount; resolved by getReplyPreviews and never embedded in a Message

`MessageContextPage`messages (newest first) plus olderCursor and newerCursor, each null when the window reached that end of the room

`MessageMedia`ImageMedia, FileMedia, LocationMedia, and ContactMedia

`InboxSummary`latestMessage (at most its first 4 media, null for an empty room), unreadCount, unreadCountCapped, readPosition, lastReadAt, activityAt, plus trailing unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion and isUnread (derived when omitted, so existing literals keep their badges)

`ConversationPrivateState / ClearUnreadResult`conversationId, unreadMarkedAt, privateStateVersion; ClearUnreadResult adds cleared

`InboxEntry / InboxPage`InboxEntry carries conversation (participants limited to 10) beside the summary fields and a summary accessor; InboxPage carries entries and nextCursor (null on the last page)

`Realtime events`MessageEvent (type INSERT or UPDATE, message), MessageDeletedEvent (id, conversationId), TypingEvent, ReadEvent (userId, readAt, readPosition), PresenceEvent, and connection status

`ConvoKitException`Stable code (for example MESSAGE\_NOT\_FOUND for a read whose target is not in the conversation or for a message the caller cannot see, REVISION\_CONFLICT with status 409 for an editMessage whose revision is stale, INVALID\_ARGUMENT for an inbox limit outside 1..100, a negative privateStateVersion or ifVersion, or a negative revision, all before any request, or INVALID\_CURSOR with status 400 for a cursor ConvoKit did not issue), optional HTTP status, response body, and cause

### Session lifecycle

Connect the user before creating subscriptions or SDK-backed UI. Your token provider must fetch fresh tokens from your authenticated backend.

On sign-out or account change, dispose the current UI controllers and subscriptions, then disconnect the client. Create a new adapter or controller after the next successful login, even when signing back in as the same user.

See [authentication](https://convokit.app/docs/auth) for the token flow and [messaging behavior](https://convokit.app/docs/messaging) for read receipts, retries, timestamps, and what the SDK-backed UI handles automatically.
